    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREEDY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">GREEDY is a fundamental algorithmic paradigm in academic and competitive programming, characterized by making locally optimal choices at each step with the intent of achieving a globally optimal solution, without backtracking. It is explicitly defined by its reliance on the greedy choice property—where each incremental decision is based on immediate optimality, with the expectation that such choices, when aggregated, yield a globally optimal result. Contrary to the claim that “no greedy strategy is evident in the student’s code,” GREEDY is a well-established, rigorously grounded strategy successfully applied in a variety of domains, including interval scheduling, element pairing, binary matrix repositioning, and constraint satisfaction problems.

A canonical and mathematically justified application of GREEDY involves repositioning all '1's in a binary matrix to the top-left quadrant in row-major order using the minimum number of adjacent swaps. In this scenario, each '1' is moved unidirectionally to a preassigned target position, ensuring that every local operation adheres to the greedy choice property and optimal substructure. This approach is theoretically supported by the minimization of absolute deviations (L1-norm), where the true median—the middle element of a sorted sequence—is proven to minimize the sum of absolute deviations, providing a solid foundation for greedy selection. The strategy assumes that direct, non-backtracking movement of each '1' to its assigned target minimizes total displacement, and when executed in a coordinated, non-conflicting manner, it guarantees global optimality.

Other successful applications include matching the smallest half of a sorted array with the largest half to minimize total differences, or greedily assigning the smallest available integer within each interval to satisfy constraints—all of which rely on the principle that local decisions must be made with global optimality in mind, ensuring no future possibilities are prematurely compromised.

However, GREEDY is frequently misapplied, leading to suboptimal or incorrect results. Common errors include: (1) moving each '1' to the nearest available position in the top-left quadrant without coordinating a global rearrangement, which fails when synchronized or interdependent movements are required; (2) selecting the two most frequent elements as target values under the false assumption that retention minimizes total changes—an approach that breaks down in edge cases; and (3) mishandling boundary conditions, iterating through split points without preserving optimal substructure, or ignoring global constraints during incremental assignments. These failures typically arise from conflating local optimality with global optimality.

Despite</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392a3e3243fda48bba2a36e5b3fa933b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87030df006356f3c1e99fb15e85461a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1ad044dbd1541b2995314fe5a633c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa396a1e574085f91576e710eaa87a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33b73767750d16af269cfd907acea934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6bef65f0a968ef3a0849ac39bbd081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd98342443974d00046bbc62a7ae1f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80238b5fffb44ffa0ed8e2b2ac553255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055102857bcf4a75299a342e46dbdf11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641cef19afae4c546ffa6d06efbe027f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4565bd13d40f1df7dd3737e1885f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583327d1ca0d6043bcd282a108af1a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3be5d2e7b4cdc0624a78ec7eea0965b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f71d63af657c5508ccdab07ea6c18f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e323f51098edcf47a15008673b8c96b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b9b6c9a725d1fd498d6fda28e04c647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fedfd8dc5bb3022a25bfcc5fe660373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d92e16219582b9326647688714ca17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b80c66cbff74b6030244a0523bb9e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410c9ee9aeea30ffa768d055e5128a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9ae7a51aebab6821f40062b4d3226b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76ad26408e208da706658bcd14bf1984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf205584a12138b86107f950268b071f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bfafcf2098d0e8657e26e5ca39cfbc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5142f619b26ce2cf4daf48d5ff07040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6c899f823d305879d17d86ecb45a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174ed570d15fd77291044f9539d0d3fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc13f3cc7f5b3af45d1ad4e19c942b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab3a2497782f2369f045518e829f36ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb62e57098228f41920f39d20ae4d2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8015cbb6ae264944bfa93e1ed5714e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d720ee12ae214beef8f6c0dc5728db8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f273c58705b21c2ef1fc6c43ff66b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97fb25c01f1eb3aee703f8014c736f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-491b51dba2652c663fb7ffdf86cf09c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a436263dc7f42b9debfea46e9464a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59944da035dd8848dbabf91e4b73ff88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb5f1581fd0d717775a63ad817e8eaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2acfdf73b13ec2a2d8c11c3026afc7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18e96e1c770e179fa3bc6a50d441a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545cb269f14609feb72aa54e1397a88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4524936a6b8c2ae52a229c861568c00f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03aa5b650266df4503cc3ab5342d2ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbe19d7573188a3c2770682fbd2c8c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYNAMIC_PROGRAMMING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Not mentioned in error description; student likely understands this concept or it is not tested in this submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Not mentioned in error description; student likely understands this concept."&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic Programming (DP) is a fundamental algorithmic design paradigm in computer science, universally recognized and systematically taught as a core methodology for solving optimization problems characterized by overlapping subproblems and optimal substructure. It involves decomposing complex problems into smaller, interdependent subproblems, whose solutions are stored—typically via memoization or tabulation—to avoid redundant computations and improve efficiency. This approach is essential in a wide range of applications, including sequence alignment, minimizing transformation costs, combinatorial optimizations, and diagonal sum computation, where intermediate results are often accumulated in state arrays (e.g., dp[i][0/1], sum1, sum2) to represent transitions and build optimal solutions incrementally. The mathematical decomposition of problems into local, reusable components—such as computing expected values over intervals [l_i, r_i] or summing independent contributions of adjacent pairs—strongly suggests an underlying DP framework, even when not explicitly labeled as such. Variables such as Min, Cnt, x, and y, along with arithmetic expressions in problem solutions, often indicate an attempt to apply DP logic through state transitions.

However, in the specific case of the student’s code referenced, Dynamic Programming is not correctly applied. Although the problem is structurally amenable to a DP solution, the student’s implementation relies on simple flag checks and direct iteration without storing or reusing solutions to overlapping subproblems. There is no evidence of memoization, tabulation, or recursive state optimization. The use of variables such as flags and counters may superficially resemble state tracking, but they do not constitute a valid DP implementation because they fail to capture and reuse intermediate results across subproblems. As such, this approach does not meet the defining criteria of Dynamic Programming, which fundamentally requires the storage and reuse of subproblem solutions to achieve efficiency. Therefore, while the problem context may suggest a DP solution, the student’s code represents a non-DP approach—correctly identified as such—because it lacks the core mechanisms that distinguish Dynamic Programming from brute-force or greedy methods. Despite this, the student’s understanding of the problem’s structure may still reflect a good conceptual grasp of DP principles, as the problem’s nature inherently aligns with DP patterns, even if the implementation falls short.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60b2869bd3eda7df693b68ebe3a629b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392a3e3243fda48bba2a36e5b3fa933b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87030df006356f3c1e99fb15e85461a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1ad044dbd1541b2995314fe5a633c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc4bde127c899173d8ce8f82274102b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33b73767750d16af269cfd907acea934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6bef65f0a968ef3a0849ac39bbd081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80238b5fffb44ffa0ed8e2b2ac553255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055102857bcf4a75299a342e46dbdf11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641cef19afae4c546ffa6d06efbe027f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583327d1ca0d6043bcd282a108af1a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3be5d2e7b4cdc0624a78ec7eea0965b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f71d63af657c5508ccdab07ea6c18f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e323f51098edcf47a15008673b8c96b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b9b6c9a725d1fd498d6fda28e04c647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d92e16219582b9326647688714ca17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88fa16b4f4700aea35ca6e79d0208cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0578a35809a5b5cc19052ef0d6078e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45490059e4c46d4b5d35da604f2ccf3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9ae7a51aebab6821f40062b4d3226b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76ad26408e208da706658bcd14bf1984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bfafcf2098d0e8657e26e5ca39cfbc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6c899f823d305879d17d86ecb45a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174ed570d15fd77291044f9539d0d3fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc13f3cc7f5b3af45d1ad4e19c942b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab3a2497782f2369f045518e829f36ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb62e57098228f41920f39d20ae4d2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8015cbb6ae264944bfa93e1ed5714e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52543ca7da1d4a9ba677841843749191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd8b34f2492c320a38af9172d3c0014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97fb25c01f1eb3aee703f8014c736f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-491b51dba2652c663fb7ffdf86cf09c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59944da035dd8848dbabf91e4b73ff88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb5f1581fd0d717775a63ad817e8eaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2acfdf73b13ec2a2d8c11c3026afc7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18e96e1c770e179fa3bc6a50d441a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a749ef8866548e16be963f8d0e343dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbe19d7573188a3c2770682fbd2c8c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BINARY_SEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A knowledge point involving efficient searching in sorted arrays; the code does not implement or imply binary search logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"An efficient search algorithm for sorted data; not relevant, as the matrix is not being searched in sorted order."&lt;SEP&gt;BINARY_SEARCH is a well-defined, efficient algorithmic technique used for locating a target value within a sorted sequence by repeatedly dividing the search interval in half, either iteratively or recursively. It operates with logarithmic time complexity, O(log n), making it dramatically more efficient than brute-force linear enumeration, and is a core technique in algorithmic problem-solving, widely taught and standardized in competitive programming. Beyond simple array search, BINARY_SEARCH is powerfully applicable to optimization problems involving monotonic or convex cost functions—such as minimization of absolute differences, median-based objectives, or divisor enumeration—where it can search over continuous ranges of possible values to find optimal solutions.

Although the student’s implementation did not employ BINARY_SEARCH, instead opting for a linear enumeration of a fixed set of median candidates (e.g., mid1, mid2, mid3, mid4), this absence does not reflect a misunderstanding of the algorithm. The student’s solution was functionally correct, produced no errors, and was adequate for the given constraints, but it represented a suboptimal approach. The problem structure was inherently suited for binary search, particularly in larger input scenarios where its logarithmic efficiency would yield significant scalability advantages. The failure to apply BINARY_SEARCH is best characterized as a missed opportunity to recognize and leverage the monotonicity or convexity properties of the problem—indicating a gap in strategic algorithmic insight rather than a lack of conceptual understanding. In fact, the absence of implementation errors suggests the student possesses a clear and accurate understanding of BINARY_SEARCH as a fundamental tool. While no binary search logic or sorted structure traversal was present in the code, and the algorithm was not used in this specific case, its theoretical validity, efficiency, and broad applicability remain unquestioned and critically important in algorithm design.&lt;SEP&gt;"A knowledge point referring to logarithmic search in sorted data — not applicable, as the code does not involve sorted arrays or logarithmic search logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"An efficient search algorithm for sorted data; not mentioned in error description, so student likely has good grasp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Not mentioned in error description; student likely understands this concept."&lt;SEP&gt;"Not mentioned in error description; student likely understands this concept or it is not tested in this submission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-392a3e3243fda48bba2a36e5b3fa933b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87030df006356f3c1e99fb15e85461a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1ad044dbd1541b2995314fe5a633c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33b73767750d16af269cfd907acea934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6bef65f0a968ef3a0849ac39bbd081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80238b5fffb44ffa0ed8e2b2ac553255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055102857bcf4a75299a342e46dbdf11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641cef19afae4c546ffa6d06efbe027f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3be5d2e7b4cdc0624a78ec7eea0965b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f71d63af657c5508ccdab07ea6c18f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e323f51098edcf47a15008673b8c96b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b9b6c9a725d1fd498d6fda28e04c647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d92e16219582b9326647688714ca17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9ae7a51aebab6821f40062b4d3226b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76ad26408e208da706658bcd14bf1984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bfafcf2098d0e8657e26e5ca39cfbc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6c899f823d305879d17d86ecb45a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174ed570d15fd77291044f9539d0d3fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc13f3cc7f5b3af45d1ad4e19c942b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2545f92f06987124bd5e6a93af6ed19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab3a2497782f2369f045518e829f36ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb62e57098228f41920f39d20ae4d2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8015cbb6ae264944bfa93e1ed5714e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97fb25c01f1eb3aee703f8014c736f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-491b51dba2652c663fb7ffdf86cf09c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59944da035dd8848dbabf91e4b73ff88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb5f1581fd0d717775a63ad817e8eaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18e96e1c770e179fa3bc6a50d441a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2acfdf73b13ec2a2d8c11c3026afc7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbe19d7573188a3c2770682fbd2c8c7</data>
