    <node id="&quot;[L_I, R_I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"[l_i, r_i] denotes the constrained range for the i-th element in the permutation, specifying the minimum and maximum allowable integer values for each position in the array."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the constrained range for the i-th element in the permutation, specifying the minimum and maximum allowable values for each position in the array."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the inclusive range constraint for the i-th element in the permutation, defining allowable integer values for each position in the array."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] is the constrained range for the i-th element in the permutation, specifying the allowable minimum and maximum values each position can take."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the inclusive integer interval from which each element a_i is independently and uniformly randomly generated, forming the probabilistic domain of the sequence."</data>
