    <node id="&quot;MASTERY LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mastery Level is a derived metric reflecting the student’s proficiency on a specific problem based on their submission and accompanying error description, though not explicitly stated, it is implied by 'Good' or 'Bad' labels."&lt;SEP&gt;Mastery Level is an evaluative metric derived from the analysis of a student’s specific problem submission, reflecting their proficiency and depth of understanding of the underlying knowledge points. It is determined solely by examining the student’s program code and the associated error description for that particular submission, without reference to prior submissions or overall performance. The metric infers the student’s grasp of specific concepts based on whether errors are present or absent, and how those errors relate to the correct or incorrect application of knowledge. In some cases, it is further informed by the classification of the submission as “Good” or “Bad,” but its core determination relies on the qualitative analysis of the error description and the correctness of the response. Mastery Level is not a general measure of ability, but a targeted, submission-specific assessment designed to guide precise educational feedback by identifying gaps or strengths in the student’s understanding of the problem at hand.&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastery Level is a qualitative or quantitative measure of the student’s grasp of the knowledge points, derived solely from the evaluation of their submission and accompanying error description."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4107cad195311f65a1ddf5c1465e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-004ef4fc2ed15929827169f862ebd088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3673ec7f6a5b2f3e304250e6b8edbb07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccea04d305753de718ec8196bbb4d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aee1cb5b4db6b902a5def2f1b55fc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c667d557d4fb1e9f0b759d48acec31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24a1b23c6ef98a895ddcdfb7da26877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-858d6fd6c77203154ce8dd3aac59f898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7258c56b189afe5558686950c289cc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d435920a0aa88626e8ac90d92c72f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-448e4914a3aacbe6e90e6ab1a7e58ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f6a2bc11c533aa2060f9b83958aa249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174472b84d2963740d25777960a64885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-658b2c72d54f5635fe092e1d409216ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb545e46aabe21f67de0b3e0da010f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A problem is a specific task or question presented to a student, against which their submission is evaluated for mastery of underlying knowledge points."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific academic problem or task that the student attempted to solve, whose performance is being evaluated based on their submission and error analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The problem is a specific educational task or exercise that the student is attempting to solve, whose difficulty and requirements inform the assessment of mastery level."&lt;SEP&gt;"Problem refers to the specific academic task or question the student attempted to solve, whose submission is being analyzed for errors and mastery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-858d6fd6c77203154ce8dd3aac59f898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-658b2c72d54f5635fe092e1d409216ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5291e8c8d87427d45354665dbecd763b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBMISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Submission is the act of a student providing a response to a problem, which is then analyzed for errors to determine mastery of knowledge points."&lt;SEP&gt;"Submission is the student's response to the problem, which includes their program code and error description, used to assess understanding and mastery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Submission refers to the student's completed work or response to a problem, which is evaluated using the 'Good'/'Bad' framework and error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"Submission refers to the student's individual attempt at solving the problem, including their program code and any associated error descriptions, which are evaluated independently to determine mastery level."&lt;SEP&gt;"The act of the student submitting their solution to the problem, which is analyzed independently to assess program correctness and error patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Submission refers to the act of the student providing their response to the problem, which is analyzed for errors to determine mastery level."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ccea04d305753de718ec8196bbb4d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-858d6fd6c77203154ce8dd3aac59f898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5291e8c8d87427d45354665dbecd763b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d435920a0aa88626e8ac90d92c72f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-658b2c72d54f5635fe092e1d409216ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDUCATIONAL ASSESSMENT SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An educational assessment system is a structured platform or framework used to evaluate student performance through automated analysis of submissions, error descriptions, and mastery indicators like 'Good' and 'Bad'."&lt;SEP&gt;"An educational assessment system is the framework or platform used to record, track, and evaluate student submissions such as programs and error descriptions, using record IDs and timestamps."&lt;SEP&gt;"An educational assessment system is the implied infrastructure that collects, tracks, and evaluates student submissions such as Record ID 43-1, using error descriptions and program analysis to determine mastery levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"The educational assessment system is the underlying framework or platform that records, tracks, and evaluates student submissions using identifiers like 37-1 and timestamps to ensure accurate and independent assessment of mastery levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"An educational assessment system is the inferred framework that collects, tracks, and evaluates student submissions like Record ID 93-1, using program code and error descriptions to determine mastery levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Educational Assessment System is the overarching framework or platform that collects, evaluates, and tracks student submissions using indicators like 'Good' and 'Bad' to measure mastery levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Educational Assessment System is the framework or platform that collects, tracks, and evaluates student submissions using Record IDs, timestamps, and error indicators like 'Good' and 'Bad'."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Educational Assessment System is the framework or platform used to collect, track, and evaluate student submissions such as Record ID: 107-2, using indicators like 'Good' and 'Bad' to measure understanding."</data>
