    <node id="&quot;KNOWLEDGE POINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Knowledge Points are specific concepts or skills being assessed in a student's submission; their presence or absence in error descriptions determines the inferred level of understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Points refer to a curated list of conceptual or procedural criteria used to evaluate student understanding in an educational assessment context, serving as a framework for grading accuracy and comprehension."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the specific concepts or skills being tested in the student's program; they serve as the evaluative framework for determining mastery levels based on correctness of response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points are the core concepts or learning objectives from a list that are relevant to evaluating student performance on a given problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points are conceptual elements from a predefined list that are relevant to the problem, used to evaluate the student's comprehension and application in their program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Points refer to specific educational concepts or skills being assessed in a student's submission; their presence or absence in error descriptions determines the student's mastery level."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific learning objectives or content areas that are assessed in student submissions; absence of error description implies mastery, while mention implies potential misunderstanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points are the underlying concepts or skills assessed in a problem; their presence or absence in the error description determines whether the student has mastered them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the specific concepts or skills being assessed in a student's submission, used as criteria to determine mastery level."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Points refer to a structured list of conceptual or procedural criteria used to evaluate student understanding in an educational assessment context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the underlying concepts or skills assessed in the problem; their absence in the error description implies the student has mastered them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Points refer to a set of defined educational criteria or concepts used to evaluate student understanding, typically aligned with curriculum objectives or learning outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to specific concepts or skills being assessed in a student's submission, used as criteria to determine mastery level based on error presence or absence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points are specific concepts or skills being assessed in a problem; their presence or absence in error descriptions determines whether a student has demonstrated understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Points refer to the specific concepts or skills being assessed in a problem; their mastery is inferred from whether the student's submission contains errors or not."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Points refer to the specific concepts or skills being assessed in the problem; their mastery is inferred from whether the student's submission contains errors or not."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4107cad195311f65a1ddf5c1465e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa51ab7e65d356229972d6750fbc73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-004ef4fc2ed15929827169f862ebd088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ae858b750790591a327c7d142473ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccea04d305753de718ec8196bbb4d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aee1cb5b4db6b902a5def2f1b55fc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c667d557d4fb1e9f0b759d48acec31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29586db94ae4094fb3286e4239680fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7258c56b189afe5558686950c289cc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d435920a0aa88626e8ac90d92c72f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174472b84d2963740d25777960a64885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-658b2c72d54f5635fe092e1d409216ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb545e46aabe21f67de0b3e0da010f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4db67f6f26be9e4b4ab88e308dd16a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOOD: [DESCRIPTION]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'Good: [description]' is a structured evaluation format used to confirm that a student has correctly understood the knowledge point, with the description elaborating on the demonstrated understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Good: [description]' is a structured evaluation label indicating the student correctly understood the problem, demonstrated by absence of errors or accurate self-correction in the error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Good: [description]' is an evaluative output format used to indicate the student correctly understood the knowledge point, as inferred from absence of errors or explicit confirmation of correctness."&lt;SEP&gt;"A structured feedback format used to indicate that a student demonstrates understanding of a concept, typically when no error is described in the submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Good: [description]' is a structured output format used to evaluate student understanding, where the description elaborates on the correct application of knowledge points."&lt;SEP&gt;"Good: [description] is a formatted evaluation output indicating the student correctly understood a knowledge point, as inferred from absence of errors or explicit confirmation of correctness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-004ef4fc2ed15929827169f862ebd088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c667d557d4fb1e9f0b759d48acec31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7258c56b189afe5558686950c289cc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29586db94ae4094fb3286e4239680fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD: [DESCRIPTION]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'Bad: [description]' is a formatted indicator used to denote that a student's submission contains errors or demonstrates misunderstanding of the knowledge point, based on provided error descriptions."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Bad: [description]' is an evaluative output format used to indicate the student misunderstood or failed to grasp the knowledge point, as inferred from explicit error details in the description."&lt;SEP&gt;"A structured feedback format used to indicate a student’s incorrect answer, containing specific error details to diagnose misunderstanding in problem-solving."&lt;SEP&gt;"A structured feedback format used to indicate that a student's answer contains errors, signaling a misunderstanding or lack of understanding of the knowledge point."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Bad: [description]' is a structured evaluation label indicating the student misunderstood the problem, as evidenced by explicit error details in the description."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Bad: [description]' is a structured output format used to evaluate student misunderstanding, where the description details the nature of the error or conceptual flaw."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bad: [description] is a formatted evaluation output indicating the student misunderstood or failed to grasp a knowledge point, as inferred from explicit error details in their description."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Bad: [description]' is a structured evaluation format used to identify that a student has misunderstood or incorrectly applied the knowledge point, with the description detailing the nature of the error."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4107cad195311f65a1ddf5c1465e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-004ef4fc2ed15929827169f862ebd088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c667d557d4fb1e9f0b759d48acec31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7258c56b189afe5558686950c289cc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29586db94ae4094fb3286e4239680fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a15e660cbb80bfae0b9863f969116c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N行N列01矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n行n列01矩阵是问题的输入结构，代表一个二维网格空间，其中每个位置为'0'或'1'，需通过相邻交换操作转化为好矩阵。"&lt;SEP&gt;"n行n列01矩阵是问题的输入结构，由字符'0'和'1'组成，需通过相邻交换操作转化为好矩阵，是操作的初始对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dd2069b32b3ad84665dc044ac51f497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf205584a12138b86107f950268b071f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;43-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"43-1 is a record identifier used to track a specific student submission for evaluation, likely within an educational or assessment system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ccb545e46aabe21f67de0b3e0da010f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 17:29:29&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2025-01-21 17:29:29 is the timestamp marking the exact moment when the student submission with Record ID 43-1 was recorded, indicating when the evaluation context was captured."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ccb545e46aabe21f67de0b3e0da010f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Evaluation is the process of analyzing the student’s program and error description to determine understanding of knowledge points, resulting in 'Good:' or 'Bad:' labels for each relevant point."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ccb545e46aabe21f67de0b3e0da010f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N 行 N 列矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"‘n 行 n 列矩阵’是问题中的核心数据结构，具有偶数维度，被划分为四个相等区域，左上角为全‘1’，其余为全‘0’，是学生需要通过操作转换的目标结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"该矩阵是问题中的核心数据结构，由字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，行数和列数均为偶数，需通过操作转化为满足特定区域分布的‘好矩阵’。"&lt;SEP&gt;"该矩阵是问题中的核心数据结构，由字符'0'和'1'构成，行数和列数均为偶数，需被重新排列以满足特定区域分布条件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f7559a33bedc5f901d766c18542da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4524936a6b8c2ae52a229c861568c00f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;左上、右上、左下、右下四个区域&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"这四个区域是将 n×n 矩阵平分后形成的几何分区，其中仅左上区域应全为'1'，其余为'0'，是判定好矩阵的关键空间划分。"&lt;SEP&gt;"这四个区域是将 n×n 矩阵平分后形成的地理分区，其中仅左上区域应全为 '1'，其余为 '0'，是判断矩阵是否为‘好矩阵’的空间标准。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98f7559a33bedc5f901d766c18542da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4524936a6b8c2ae52a229c861568c00f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;相邻字符交换操作&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"这是小红允许的唯一操作，指交换矩阵中两个相邻（上下或左右）位置的字符，用于逐步将矩阵转化为好矩阵。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4524936a6b8c2ae52a229c861568c00f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Points refer to key concepts or criteria listed in a problem context, used to evaluate student understanding based on their program and error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"Points refer to key elements or criteria listed in a problem context, likely representing learning objectives or conceptual checkpoints relevant to evaluating student understanding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa51ab7e65d356229972d6750fbc73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4db67f6f26be9e4b4ab88e308dd16a1</data>
    </node>
