    <node id="&quot;N 行 N 列 01 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"‘n 行 n 列 01 矩阵’是一个二维网格结构，仅由字符‘0’和‘1’组成，其规模为 n×n，且 n 为偶数，用于表示需要被转换为‘好矩阵’的输入数据空间。"&lt;SEP&gt;"这是一个抽象的数学结构，由 n 行 n 列的字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，是问题操作的目标对象，其变换规则由小红定义。"&lt;SEP&gt;"这是一个数学构造的二维网格结构，具有 n 行 n 列（n 为偶数），由字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，是问题操作的目标对象，其空间结构被划分为四个相等的象限。"&lt;SEP&gt;"这是一个数学构造的二维网格结构，大小为 n×n，仅包含字符 '0' 和 '1'，其空间布局被划分为四个象限区域，用于定义‘好矩阵’的条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"‘n 行 n 列 01 矩阵’是问题中的核心数据结构，其大小为 n×n，仅由字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，且 n 为偶数，用于判断和转化是否符合‘好矩阵’条件的几何区域划分。"&lt;SEP&gt;"该矩阵是问题的核心数据结构，具有 n 行 n 列，仅由 '0' 和 '1' 构成，且 n 为偶数，目标是将其转换为左上角为全 '1'、其余为全 '0' 的特定布局。"&lt;SEP&gt;"这是一个数学结构，代表一个正方形网格，由字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，行数和列数均为偶数，目标是通过交换相邻元素使其满足特定区域分布条件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c84eba6b6eff8493a43c7fd384677acc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c45ae6d217837b0ec49eaf31b3f5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246822371b4a88626131f0e16a7011d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd35d2da3ec05d7b2e867504beda050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cdb2064474980b06343cd68cff259c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f97b7273e9cd49bbbd3b2dcef862908b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6ae6c968489276c8bb614966bd0f46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM_SOLVING_EVENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Problem_Solving_Event refers to the context of a student submitting a solution to an algorithmic problem, where mastery of specific knowledge points is assessed based on correctness and error analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b9b6c9a725d1fd498d6fda28e04c647</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N行N列矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n行n列矩阵是问题操作的二维空间载体，其几何结构被划分为四个相等区域，用于定义好矩阵的条件，是问题求解的物理和逻辑基础。"&lt;SEP&gt;"n行n列矩阵是问题操作的空间载体，其几何结构被划分为四个相等的象限，是实现‘好矩阵’目标的物理和逻辑区域。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26ade306a8bffa48f05220f8acafd11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a588519a4b977de5b0bcf8ded42f8642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;交换相邻字符操作&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"这是小红允许的唯一操作，指在矩阵中交换两个相邻（上下或左右）位置的字符，用于逐步将矩阵转化为好矩阵。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98f7559a33bedc5f901d766c18542da6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERATION BOUNDS: N³/2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The constraint limiting the maximum number of adjacent swaps allowed to transform the matrix, ensuring the solution is efficient and feasible within polynomial time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98f7559a33bedc5f901d766c18542da6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAM SEGMENT 2/2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a code segment written by the student, containing a loop that outputs paired swap operations. It is part of a larger solution attempting to solve the matrix transformation problem, but exhibits incorrect output formatting by printing four coordinates per line without proper validation of pairings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c84eba6b6eff8493a43c7fd384677acc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;01矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"01矩阵是问题输入的数据结构，由字符'0'和'1'构成的n行n列矩阵，是小红需要通过交换操作转化为好矩阵的初始对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b814718769c7c5ff34fd8d9992e16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERATION: SWAP ADJACENT CHARACTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is the allowed operation in the problem: exchanging two neighboring elements in the matrix, used as the sole means to transform the input matrix into a 'good matrix'."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cdb2064474980b06343cd68cff259c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEFT-UPPER REGION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The left-upper region is the top-left quadrant of the n×n matrix, defined as cells where 1 ≤ i,j ≤ n/2, and must contain all '1's in a good matrix."&lt;SEP&gt;"The left-upper region refers to the top-left quadrant of the n×n matrix, defined by coordinates 1 ≤ i,j ≤ n/2, which must contain all '1's in a 'good matrix'."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c45ae6d217837b0ec49eaf31b3f5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cdb2064474980b06343cd68cff259c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER THREE REGIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The other three regions — right-upper, left-lower, and right-lower — are the remaining quadrants of the matrix, each of size (n/2)×(n/2), and must contain only '0's in a good matrix."&lt;SEP&gt;"The other three regions — right-upper, left-lower, and right-lower — constitute the remaining three quadrants of the matrix, which must contain only '0's in a 'good matrix'."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c45ae6d217837b0ec49eaf31b3f5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cdb2064474980b06343cd68cff259c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N³/2 OPERATION LIMIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is the constraint on the maximum number of adjacent swaps allowed to transform the matrix, ensuring the solution is efficient and within a provable bound."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cdb2064474980b06343cd68cff259c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SORTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sorting is a fundamental algorithmic process used to arrange data in a specific order; the student's submission does not indicate any error, suggesting good understanding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bb5f1581fd0d717775a63ad817e8eaf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADJACENT SWAP OPERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The adjacent swap operation is the only allowed transformation, where two horizontally or vertically neighboring characters in the matrix are exchanged; this is the fundamental action used to rearrange the matrix towards the good matrix state."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c45ae6d217837b0ec49eaf31b3f5388</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N³/2 OPERATION BOUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The n³/2 operation bound is a theoretical upper limit on the number of adjacent swaps allowed to solve the problem, ensuring the solution is computationally feasible and within polynomial time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c45ae6d217837b0ec49eaf31b3f5388</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;牛可乐&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">牛可乐是多位算法与数学问题的提出者，其研究贡献主要集中在两个独立但各自完整的问题方向：字符串理论与离散结构（砖块矩阵）。在字符串处理领域，牛可乐首次定义了“字符串可爱度”的概念，并围绕该定义系统性地设计了一系列具有挑战性的算法与数学问题，包括：判定长度为 n 的字符串是否存在可爱度恰好为 m 的情况；构造满足特定可爱度条件的字符串；以及判断是否存在一个字符串 t，使得其某个子串与某个不连续子序列相等。这些问题不仅涉及字符串的结构分析，还融合了组合数学与算法设计，体现了牛可乐在问题建模与理论创新方面的深厚能力。在离散结构领域，牛可乐提出了“蓝色极大连通块”的概念，并构建了相关的算法问题，要求计算使该连通块从砖块矩阵中掉落所需敲碎的最少灰色砖块数量，展现了其在图论与动态规划等方向的深刻洞察。尽管多个描述重复提及字符串“可爱度”相关问题，但并无实质矛盾；相反，这些重复强化了牛可乐在该领域的核心贡献。总体而言，牛可乐作为多产的出题者，在算法设计、组合优化与形式化建模方面展现出广泛而深入的影响力，其工作横跨字符串理论与离散结构两大方向，为算法竞赛与理论研究提供了丰富的问题素材与研究范式。</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-304a22c33987a0af2f7be4a2bf524b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fa125bb3155fa56767ea43a710e6a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b83f56a940f8f89dfbd7fb5630b525&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad12dbd91d84d77d978a49fdce06b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9fb229ccaa906b2924ad98647d19313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f7b94d5736abea4b1f3639f0bda773f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14a39faa60f3b7fe091f2aa3abd4d35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f9a3d5c32f41f88e9433f1e6a2e55a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69050e55a85da20b5c9fbeb8e6467fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67eed4167be71f6d488c596375abffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cda7805225fd6f7e86669bb03b93656d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ed4955719b894156cc66d8c640e8a45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c5a9f768d5896586a40aa9a5d5e578d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec4fb3453fbb729dbac9f6d54953070e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baad8f7b48afed8fdda54dc328952cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;蓝色极大连通块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"蓝色极大连通块是指在矩阵中由四连通的蓝色砖块构成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是问题核心的计算目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块组成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是问题核心的计算目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块构成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是问题核心的计算目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块组成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是问题核心的计算对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;灰色砖块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"灰色砖块是可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或使蓝色极大连通块掉落，其数量和位置是计算最少敲碎次数的关键输入。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或移除蓝色极大连通块，其数量和位置决定蓝色连通块是否能掉落，是计算最少敲碎数的关键对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或移除蓝色极大连通块，其数量和位置决定连通块是否能掉落，是问题中的可操作变量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或移除蓝色极大连通块，其数量和位置决定连通块是否能掉落，是问题中的可操作元素。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;蓝色砖块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可被敲碎的砖块，以蓝色斜线绘制，构成蓝色极大连通块的基本单元，通过四连通关系形成连通区域。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可被敲碎的砖块，以蓝色斜线绘制，通过四连通形成蓝色极大连通块，是问题中需要被分离和分析的对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可被敲碎的砖块，以蓝色斜线绘制，构成蓝色极大连通块的组成部分，其连通性决定了连通块的结构。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N \TIMES M 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n \times m 矩阵是砖块的二维排列结构，由 n 行 m 列组成，用于建模蓝色砖块和灰色砖块的空间分布，是问题的物理载体。"&lt;SEP&gt;"n \times m 矩阵是砖块的二维排布结构，由 n 行 m 列组成，用于定义砖块位置 (i,j) 和分析连通块的几何基础。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;(I,J)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"(i,j) is a coordinate pair denoting a specific cell in the grid map, where i is the row index (top to bottom) and j is the column index (left to right), used to reference monster counts a_{i,j}."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i is the row (top to bottom) and j is the column (left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) 是矩阵中砖块的坐标表示法，i 表示从上往下的行号，j 表示从左往右的列号，用于精确定位每个砖块的位置。"&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) 是矩阵中砖块的坐标表示法，i 表示从上往下的行号，j 表示从左往右的列号，用于精确标识每个砖块的位置。"&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) 是表示砖块矩阵中位置的坐标系统，i 为行索引（从上往下），j 为列索引（从左往右），用于精确标识每个砖块的物理位置。"&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is the coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i denotes the row (top to bottom) and j denotes the column (left to right), forming the basis for monster placement and attack targeting."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i is the row index (top to bottom) and j is the column index (left to right), used to locate monster counts a_{i,j}."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i is the row index (top to bottom) and j is the column index (left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i is the row index (top to bottom) and j is the column index (left to right)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-79d74783b73ceb32dae708b26591e446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16239776332d396b902352ee025093cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4a7b2a080725c29db421d4e4ace60f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfc436139fa6006082f3b7f4127742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04d5bda19778e26fdcdbd138b92cbbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0abd9d06cc1108aa2d33d0668e3a2f58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;四连通&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一连通块的核心规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一连通块，是判断蓝色极大连通块的关键规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一连通块，是判断蓝色极大连通块的核心规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块是否属于同一个连通块，是判断蓝色极大连通块的核心拓扑规则。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;共边&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"共边是指两个砖块在上下左右方向上共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在上下左右方向上共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否能完好掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在上下左右方向上直接相邻共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在上下或左右方向上共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;悬空&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"悬空是指位于矩阵边界的蓝色极大连通块无需考虑其外侧无支撑的问题，是边界条件处理的特殊规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空是指蓝色极大连通块位于矩阵边界时，其外侧无砖块支撑的状态，此时不计入掉落条件，是边界处理的特殊规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空是指蓝色砖块位于矩阵边界且无其他砖块支撑，但根据规则，边界上的蓝色极大连通块无需考虑悬空问题，不影响掉落条件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;敲碎&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是使蓝色极大连通块掉落的唯一手段，问题要求计算最少敲碎次数。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是实现蓝色极大连通块脱离的唯一手段，目标是最小化敲碎次数。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是实现蓝色极大连通块掉落的唯一手段，其最小数量是问题的求解目标。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;边界&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"边界是指矩阵的外缘行或列，位于边界上的蓝色极大连通块在判断掉落条件时无需考虑外部悬空问题。"&lt;SEP&gt;"边界是指矩阵的外边缘，位于边界上的蓝色极大连通块不需要考虑悬空问题，是特殊掉落条件的判定依据。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e2ed285bc34ab93459eb373d468a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BFS ALGORITHM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BFS Algorithm is a graph traversal method used to explore connected components in a grid, counting reachable cells (cnt1) and adjacent zero cells (cnt2), with optimization to track minimum cnt2 for maximum cnt1."&lt;SEP&gt;"BFS Algorithm is a graph traversal method used to explore connected components in a grid, counting valid nodes and adjacent zero-valued cells, with the goal of finding the component with maximum size and minimum adjacent zero count."&lt;SEP&gt;"BFS Algorithm is a graph traversal technique implemented in the code to explore connected components in a grid, counting reachable cells and adjacent zero cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"BFS Algorithm is the search strategy implemented by the student in their program to explore all possible transformations of n to m using breadth-first search, representing the core computational approach used."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d513b4e5ac4753a8c4299f06737d9f5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ec471dad6ce28ff96a6fd072638d9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d86f2da20705ac92182e4cb2383023c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRID SEARCH PROBLEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grid Search Problem involves analyzing a 2D binary grid to identify connected components using breadth-first search, where the solution requires tracking component size and surrounding zero cells to determine optimal output."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grid Search Problem involves analyzing a binary grid to find the largest connected component of 1s using BFS, while counting adjacent 0s as boundary cells, and selecting the component with minimal boundary when multiple largest components exist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d86f2da20705ac92182e4cb2383023c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PI is a typedef or alias for a pair of integers (likely std::pair&lt;int, int&gt;), used in the BFS queue to store grid coordinates (x, y) for traversal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"m is the target numerical value that 小L aims to achieve from n using the allowed operations."&lt;SEP&gt;M is an integer input parameter that represents the target cuteness value (可爱度) of a string t, serving as the exact required length for both a contiguous substring and a non-contiguous subsequence to be identical — a core constraint in the “Niu Ke Le” problem. This value, which must satisfy 1 ≤ M ≤ n where n is the length of the target string, decisively determines whether a valid string t can be constructed such that its maximum-length matching substring and subsequence are both precisely of length M. M is not an upper bound or auxiliary parameter but the definitive criterion for evaluating algorithmic solutions, as any valid output must achieve this exact value. While several descriptions incorrectly associate M with the number of columns in a 2D grid map related to Dragon’s Breath or BFS traversal, these references are inconsistent with the overwhelming majority of evidence and appear to be misattributions or contextual outliers. The authoritative and coherent interpretation, supported by the unified and detailed definition across multiple sources, establishes M solely as the target cuteness value governing substring-subsequence equality in the Niu Ke Le problem. Therefore, M is unambiguously defined by its role in string construction and constraint satisfaction, not by spatial or grid dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;"m represents the number of queries, a numerical parameter indicating how many independent range-based sorting and position-tracking questions are to be processed."&lt;SEP&gt;"m 表示查询次数，是一个输入参数，定义了问题中独立询问的数量边界。"&lt;SEP&gt;"m 是询问次数，作为输入参数，表示需要对排列进行的独立查询数量，是问题复杂度的重要维度。"&lt;SEP&gt;"m是查询次数，表示需要处理的独立询问数量，影响程序效率要求。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16239776332d396b902352ee025093cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4a7b2a080725c29db421d4e4ace60f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304a22c33987a0af2f7be4a2bf524b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fa125bb3155fa56767ea43a710e6a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04d5bda19778e26fdcdbd138b92cbbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2411c621877139af242bccc0cd3326b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b83f56a940f8f89dfbd7fb5630b525&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0abd9d06cc1108aa2d33d0668e3a2f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9fb229ccaa906b2924ad98647d19313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22ff6fc321d7eede1c2519238ccbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a5ffde3e6b26abceb9147a7b795dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f7b94d5736abea4b1f3639f0bda773f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14a39faa60f3b7fe091f2aa3abd4d35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f9a3d5c32f41f88e9433f1e6a2e55a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67eed4167be71f6d488c596375abffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cda7805225fd6f7e86669bb03b93656d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79d74783b73ceb32dae708b26591e446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ed4955719b894156cc66d8c640e8a45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c5a9f768d5896586a40aa9a5d5e578d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97fb25c01f1eb3aee703f8014c736f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfc436139fa6006082f3b7f4127742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec4fb3453fbb729dbac9f6d54953070e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c18434ce64bd6a6f9f22c0ce89bd936&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baad8f7b48afed8fdda54dc328952cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c242cddb305e8c965ab852377b57233</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A[VX][VY]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a[vx][vy] is a 2D array storing binary grid values (0 or 1), where 1 indicates a traversable node and 0 indicates a boundary or empty cell adjacent to components."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIS[UX][UY]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"vis[ux][uy] is a 2D boolean visitation array used to track which grid cells have been processed during BFS to prevent revisiting and infinite loops."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CNT1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"cnt1 is a counter variable tracking the number of connected 1-valued cells in the current BFS component, used to determine the largest component."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CNT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"cnt2 is a counter variable tracking the number of adjacent 0-valued cells surrounding the current BFS component, used to minimize boundary exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ans1 is a global variable storing the maximum component size found so far, used to compare and update the optimal solution during BFS iterations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Min is a global variable storing the minimum number of adjacent zero cells among all components with the maximum size, critical for determining the final output."&lt;SEP&gt;"Min 是学生程序中用于存储最少需要敲碎的灰色砖块数量的变量，代表问题的输出目标值，是算法计算结果的载体。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Min is a variable in the student's code representing a minimum value used in arithmetic calculations, likely intended to represent an optimal subcomponent in a greedy or dynamic programming approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f47b94be846baff878bf6f6f7085dd36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583327d1ca0d6043bcd282a108af1a4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"矩阵是 n 行 m 列的砖块排布结构，用于表示问题中的物理空间，其中每个位置 (i,j) 对应一个砖块，分为可敲碎的灰色砖块和不可敲碎的蓝色砖块。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;掉落&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"掉落是指蓝色极大连通块在移除必要灰色砖块后，因不再与任何灰色砖块共边而整体脱离原结构的物理过程，是问题的最终目标。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e26cd87db8b5889ee98f45461f05c972</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-23 13:47:29&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The timestamp indicating when the record was logged, representing a specific point in time associated with the submission and serving as a temporal anchor for the event."&lt;SEP&gt;"The timestamp indicating when the record was logged, representing a specific point in time associated with the submission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59944da035dd8848dbabf91e4b73ff88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;61-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A unique record identifier for a student submission, marking a specific instance of problem-solving activity and linking to the associated error analysis and mastery evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A unique record identifier for a student submission, marking a specific instance of problem-solving activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59944da035dd8848dbabf91e4b73ff88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INPUT GRID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The input grid is a 2D binary matrix (n x m) composed of 0s and 1s, where 1s represent traversable cells and 0s represent boundaries or obstacles, used as the problem's spatial domain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d86f2da20705ac92182e4cb2383023c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONNECTED COMPONENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A connected component refers to a maximal set of adjacent 1s in the grid, connected horizontally or vertically, which the BFS algorithm is designed to identify and measure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d86f2da20705ac92182e4cb2383023c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOUNDARY COUNT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boundary Count (cnt2) is the number of adjacent 0 cells surrounding a connected component of 1s, used as a tiebreaker to select the optimal component with minimal boundary when multiple largest components exist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d86f2da20705ac92182e4cb2383023c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIS ARRAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATA_STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The vis array is a 2D boolean matrix used to track visited cells during BFS traversal, preventing reprocessing and ensuring each cell is counted only once."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d86f2da20705ac92182e4cb2383023c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS1 AND MIN VARIABLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATA_STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ans1 stores the size of the largest connected component found so far, while Min stores the minimum boundary count (cnt2) associated with that size, used for optimization during component comparison."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d86f2da20705ac92182e4cb2383023c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-23 13:49:22&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The timestamp marking the submission of a student's program and error analysis, used for record-keeping and tracking performance over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-80238b5fffb44ffa0ed8e2b2ac553255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;62-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A unique record identifier for a student submission, used to distinguish and reference individual problem attempts in an educational system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-80238b5fffb44ffa0ed8e2b2ac553255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;程序段&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"程序段是学生编写的 C++ 代码片段，用于实现对砖块矩阵的广度优先搜索（BFS），以识别和计算蓝色极大连通块的最小敲碎数。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae30464427d8e7c597e77124283292d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRID SEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grid Search is the process of iterating through a 2D matrix to identify unvisited land cells and initiate BFS from each, used to find the largest connected component."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d513b4e5ac4753a8c4299f06737d9f5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAPH STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Graph Structure is implicitly represented by the 2D grid, where each cell is a node connected to its four orthogonal neighbors (up, down, left, right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 2D grid forms an implicit Graph Structure where each cell is a node with edges to its four orthogonal neighbors (up, down, left, right), enabling traversal via BFS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d513b4e5ac4753a8c4299f06737d9f5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;砖块矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"砖块矩阵是 n 行 m 列的二维结构，由灰色（可敲碎）和蓝色（不可敲碎）砖块组成，是问题建模和算法处理的载体。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOLVE()&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"solve() 是学生程序中用于解决砖块矩阵问题的核心函数，负责读取输入、计算最少敲碎数并输出结果，是程序逻辑的执行主体。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::CIN.TIE(NULLPTR),STD::COUT.TIE(NULLPTR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"该代码片段用于关闭 C++ 标准输入输出流的同步，以提升程序运行效率，是学生程序中用于优化 I/O 性能的技术手段。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29857b4f8282de50e14a24cfb03c96db</data>
    </node>
