      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A student submission refers to a single instance of a student's response to a problem, evaluated using error descriptions and associated with a Record ID and timestamp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student Submission is the act of a student providing a program and associated error description for evaluation, which is the core data point being analyzed in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"A student submission refers to the work or response provided by a student for a given problem, which is evaluated for correctness and understanding using 'Good' or 'Bad' labels and error descriptions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A student submission refers to the act of a learner providing a response or program for automated evaluation, which is analyzed for errors and classified as 'Good' or 'Bad' based on content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student Submission refers to the act or instance of a student providing a response or program for evaluation, typically accompanied by an error description or confirmation of correctness."</data>
