    <node id="&quot;GOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'Good' is used as a marker to indicate that the student demonstrates understanding of the knowledge point, with no errors present in their submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Good is an indicator used to denote that the student demonstrates understanding of the knowledge points, based on the absence of errors in their submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Good' is used as an indicator to signify that the student demonstrates understanding of the knowledge point, with no errors present in their submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Good is an indicator used to denote that a student demonstrates understanding of a concept, typically when no errors are present in their submission, such as 'No error', '无错误', or similar phrases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Good is an indicator used to denote that a student demonstrates understanding of the material, typically when no errors are present in their submission, such as 'No error', '无错误', or similar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Good is an indicator used to signify that a student demonstrates understanding of a concept, typically when no errors are present in their response, such as 'No error', '无错误', or similar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Good is an indicator used to denote that the student demonstrates understanding of the knowledge points in the problem, typically when no errors are present in the submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Good is an indicator used to denote that the student demonstrates understanding of the knowledge points in the problem, based on the absence of errors in the submission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ccea04d305753de718ec8196bbb4d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aee1cb5b4db6b902a5def2f1b55fc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a3b43879945f4f3f3c62def7b7d32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d435920a0aa88626e8ac90d92c72f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-448e4914a3aacbe6e90e6ab1a7e58ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174472b84d2963740d25777960a64885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'Bad' is a marker used in the error description format to indicate a misunderstanding or lack of understanding by the student in their submission, typically followed by a description of the error."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Bad' is used as a marker to indicate that the student has answered incorrectly, revealing a misunderstanding or lack of understanding of the knowledge point."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bad is an indicator used to denote that the student has misunderstood or lacks understanding, typically when an error description is provided in the submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Bad' is used as an indicator to signify that the student has answered incorrectly, indicating a misunderstanding or lack of understanding of the knowledge point."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bad is an indicator used to denote that a student has misunderstood or lacks understanding of a concept, typically when an error description is provided in their submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bad is an indicator used to denote that a student has misunderstood or lacks understanding, typically when an error description is provided in their submission, indicating an incorrect answer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bad is an indicator used to signify that a student has misunderstood or lacks understanding of a concept, typically when an error description is provided in their submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bad is an indicator used to denote that the student has misunderstood or lacks understanding of the knowledge points, typically when an error description is provided in the submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bad is an indicator used to denote that the student has misunderstood or lacks understanding of the knowledge points, as indicated by the presence of error details in the submission."</data>
