    <node id="&quot;NO ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'No Error' is a textual indicator used in student submissions to signify the absence of mistakes, often triggering the 'Good' classification in automated assessment systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' is a phrase used to indicate the absence of mistakes in a student's submission, signaling correct understanding or successful execution of the task."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' is a phrase used to indicate the absence of mistakes in the student's submission, signifying correct understanding or successful execution."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' is a textual indicator used to signify that a student's submission contains no detectable mistakes, supporting a 'Good' evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' is a textual indicator used in student submissions to signify the absence of mistakes, leading to a 'Good' classification of understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' is a textual indicator used in student submissions to signify the absence of mistakes, implying correct understanding of the problem or concept."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4aee1cb5b4db6b902a5def2f1b55fc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a3b43879945f4f3f3c62def7b7d32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-448e4914a3aacbe6e90e6ab1a7e58ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174472b84d2963740d25777960a64885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;无错误&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'无错误' is a Chinese-language indicator meaning 'no error', used in student submissions to confirm correct responses without mistakes."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is a Chinese-language phrase meaning 'no error,' used in student submissions to indicate correct answers and trigger the 'Good' classification in multilingual educational systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is the Chinese phrase for 'No error', used as a multilingual indicator of correct student performance in the assessment system."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is the Chinese translation of 'No error', used to denote the same condition of error-free student work in multilingual contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is the Chinese phrase for 'no error,' used equivalently to 'No error' to denote that the student's response contains no mistakes and demonstrates proper comprehension."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is a Chinese-language textual indicator used in student submissions to signify the absence of mistakes, equivalent to 'No error' and leading to a 'Good' classification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4aee1cb5b4db6b902a5def2f1b55fc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a3b43879945f4f3f3c62def7b7d32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-448e4914a3aacbe6e90e6ab1a7e58ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174472b84d2963740d25777960a64885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1</data>
    </node>
