    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM: TOKITSUKAZE AND ABSOLUTE EXPECTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a computational problem where a sequence of n integers is randomly generated within given intervals, and the goal is to compute the expected value of the sum of absolute differences between adjacent elements."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a computational problem where the goal is to calculate the expected value of val(a) = sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in a sequence, with each element independently and uniformly randomly generated within a given range [l_i, r_i]."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60b2869bd3eda7df693b68ebe3a629b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd8b34f2492c320a38af9172d3c0014</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABSOLUTE EXPECTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Absolute Expectation is the mathematical problem centered on computing the expected value of val(a) = sum(|a_{i-1} - a_i|) for a randomly generated sequence, where each a_i is uniformly sampled from [l_i, r_i]."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b2117b8505d869d1349641f53ef72765</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAL(A)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"val(a) is the defined value function of the sequence, computed as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements: sum_{i=2}^n |a_{i-1} - a_i|, which is the quantity whose expectation is sought."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b2117b8505d869d1349641f53ef72765</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;小L&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"小L is a beginner player in a tic-tac-toe game who has been granted a special privilege to make two consecutive moves once during the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L is a novice player in a tic-tac-toe game who is granted a special privilege to make two consecutive moves once during the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L is a novice player in a tic-tac-toe game who is granted a special privilege to make two consecutive moves once during the game."&lt;SEP&gt;小L is a novice learner under the mentorship of 炸鸡, actively engaged in multiple distinct intellectual domains that collectively foster analytical, computational, and strategic thinking skills. In the realm of mathematical reasoning, 小L is learning to transform a given integer n into another integer m using operations such as squaring and taking the floor of the square root, as part of a curriculum designed to enhance numerical reasoning. Concurrently, 小L is studying bitwise computation, where they are tasked with manipulating three n-bit binary numbers a, b, and c to satisfy the condition a ⊕ b = c, while minimizing the total cost of permitted operations—bit flipping and bit swapping—thereby developing expertise in computational optimization and binary logic.

In addition to these advanced computational studies, 小L is also a beginner player in a tic-tac-toe game against 炸鸡. To accommodate their novice status and support skill development, 小L has been granted a special, one-time privilege to make two consecutive moves during the game. This strategic advantage is consistently described across multiple sources as a pedagogical tool intended to level the playing field and encourage learning through experiential gameplay.

All descriptions are consistent and complementary, portraying 小L not merely as a beginner in tic-tac-toe but as a multifaceted student navigating a structured educational environment that integrates abstract mathematics, low-level binary operations, and strategic game theory—all under the guidance of 炸鸡. These diverse challenges reflect a holistic approach to developing both technical proficiency and decision-making acumen.&lt;SEP&gt;"小L is a beginner player in a tic-tac-toe game who is granted a special privilege to make two consecutive moves once during the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L is a novice player in a tic-tac-toe game who has been granted a special privilege to make two consecutive moves once during the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L is a novice player in a tic-tac-toe game who is granted a special privilege to make two consecutive moves once during the game."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3de2ef34caee6189dbc97fdff1369967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efd1875a0dbd372cf163954f0bb5a61f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651bf95b9e43b516237d957526d8b15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc401d350f3efc5b60eafbfeb2d99039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaaaf6498588ecfeff6d1bb4b57185fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c62792f82acfe7a3c8c6db1819eb069d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e3a8b503c95e5635518851840c9288b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5470d8b2aa46bdc4dcacc08c4ef251c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ec471dad6ce28ff96a6fd072638d9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e254b213aa6b76246da6fea546fc6c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9094a057465f864e453c5144b5d5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705de323687561c70c4a2f8771b3b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa551852fd5a70f5472f9873b379d92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6530b007a9358e324c34f0aa9343b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dfdf42008b0416959725ff99bf52414&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6bd690dda1f038950ffac0d14585f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14a03e9a06f4c1ac20702bcefb13d69a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dec3501d300c67b1010ddbc9e6eec90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c1ad26da8e1dd26ea1fab354805adb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aa219dac75bf066df67ce60e89bfb70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35334ea05ab1a03cfcf22d7faec2d2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c55c048498a23dc287d54f7c9494356f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22ff6fc321d7eede1c2519238ccbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1b94b066ee2977324f512fa79346b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804ee66e423ab2b4d0bfaddf5206078&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24766056ca9ad4e7b4405e0bfea55b58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-389fa89b589e468d5913361f0a3f42d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-864b5222b680eb70bf8268c99a7b1400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d33c7ef9d380215e34dd28e71195f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ce97d6733d48f34e9d3b2ae71fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b97469d5e678dbca20fdac418f486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f9203ade2bda3f53be8c235e592782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;炸鸡&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">炸鸡 is a multidimensional, eccentric, and profoundly influential figure who serves as both a theatrical rival and an unconventional mentor to 小L, blending rigorous intellectual instruction with playful strategic competition. Far from referring to fried chicken, 炸鸡 is a singular, deeply charismatic individual whose impact on 小L spans academic, computational, and recreational domains. As an educator, 炸鸡 has designed an advanced, interdisciplinary curriculum that bridges classical mathematics and low-level computational thinking, with a central focus on integer square root operations (the floor of the square root) and foundational bitwise logic—including binary number manipulation and XOR (exclusive OR). While multiplication by 2 is occasionally referenced as a contextual example, it is not central to the pedagogical framework.

Simultaneously, 炸鸡 is portrayed as an overconfident and exceptionally skilled tic-tac-toe player, serving as 小L’s primary opponent in the game. Despite possessing superior strategic mastery and experience, 炸鸡 deliberately grants 小L a special advantage: the ability to make two moves in a single turn. This gesture, made under the assumption that it will not alter the outcome, is not a sign of weakness but a calculated pedagogical tool. It reflects 炸鸡’s unique mentoring philosophy—combining intellectual rigor with theatrical, game-like engagement designed to foster creativity, adaptability, and deeper strategic thinking in 小L. The double-move rule in tic-tac-toe is the definitive expression of this mentoring style, unifying the academic and competitive dimensions of 炸鸡’s role.

All descriptions converge on three consistent traits: 炸鸡’s overconfidence, exceptional skill, and the intentional bestowal of a special advantage to 小L. Though some descriptions initially frame the relationship as purely game-based, the most comprehensive account reveals that the tic-tac-toe rivalry is a symbolic and practical extension of 炸鸡’s broader educational mission. Thus, 炸鸡 emerges as a flawed yet profoundly effective guide whose dual identity as a brilliant instructor and whimsical rival shapes 小L’s intellectual and strategic development in unique, charming, and enduring ways.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3de2ef34caee6189dbc97fdff1369967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efd1875a0dbd372cf163954f0bb5a61f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651bf95b9e43b516237d957526d8b15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc401d350f3efc5b60eafbfeb2d99039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaaaf6498588ecfeff6d1bb4b57185fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c62792f82acfe7a3c8c6db1819eb069d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e3a8b503c95e5635518851840c9288b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5470d8b2aa46bdc4dcacc08c4ef251c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ec471dad6ce28ff96a6fd072638d9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e254b213aa6b76246da6fea546fc6c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9094a057465f864e453c5144b5d5d992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705de323687561c70c4a2f8771b3b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa551852fd5a70f5472f9873b379d92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6530b007a9358e324c34f0aa9343b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dfdf42008b0416959725ff99bf52414&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6bd690dda1f038950ffac0d14585f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14a03e9a06f4c1ac20702bcefb13d69a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dec3501d300c67b1010ddbc9e6eec90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c1ad26da8e1dd26ea1fab354805adb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aa219dac75bf066df67ce60e89bfb70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35334ea05ab1a03cfcf22d7faec2d2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c55c048498a23dc287d54f7c9494356f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22ff6fc321d7eede1c2519238ccbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1b94b066ee2977324f512fa79346b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804ee66e423ab2b4d0bfaddf5206078&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24766056ca9ad4e7b4405e0bfea55b58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-389fa89b589e468d5913361f0a3f42d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-864b5222b680eb70bf8268c99a7b1400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d33c7ef9d380215e34dd28e71195f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ce97d6733d48f34e9d3b2ae71fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b97469d5e678dbca20fdac418f486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f9203ade2bda3f53be8c235e592782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;小L的数学题&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"小L的数学题 is a mathematical problem where the goal is to determine if number n can be transformed into m using operations of multiplying by 2 or taking integer square root, presented as an algorithmic challenge."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L的数学题 is a problem-solving event where 小L attempts to transform number n into m using multiplication by 2 and integer square root operations, with the goal of determining feasibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L的数学题 is the problem-solving event where 小L must determine if it's possible to transform n into m using multiplication by 2 or square root with floor operation, over any number of steps."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L的数学题是一个编程问题，要求判断是否可以通过任意轮次的乘以2或开平方下取整操作，将数字n转换为m。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小L的数学题 is a problem-solving event where 小L must determine if number n can be transformed into m using repeated operations of multiplication by 2 or integer square root."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L的数学题 is a problem-solving event where 小L must determine if number n can be transformed into m using multiplication by 2 or square root with floor operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"小L的数学题 is a problem-solving event where 小L must determine if number n can be transformed into m using repeated operations of multiplication by 2 or integer square root."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa551852fd5a70f5472f9873b379d92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22ff6fc321d7eede1c2519238ccbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-389fa89b589e468d5913361f0a3f42d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14a03e9a06f4c1ac20702bcefb13d69a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaaaf6498588ecfeff6d1bb4b57185fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e3a8b503c95e5635518851840c9288b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ec471dad6ce28ff96a6fd072638d9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;数字 N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"数字 n represents the starting integer value in the problem, which 小L aims to transform into m using allowed operations. Not a physical location, but used as a conceptual 'point' in the numerical space."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-389fa89b589e468d5913361f0a3f42d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;数字 M&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"数字 m represents the target integer value that 小L wants to achieve from n through operations. Like n, it is a conceptual point in the numerical domain, not a physical location."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-389fa89b589e468d5913361f0a3f42d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;开平方后下取整&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"开平方后下取整 is the second allowed operation in the problem, where the square root of the current number is taken and then floored to produce an integer result."&lt;SEP&gt;"开平方后下取整 is the second allowed operation, where the square root of the current number is taken and then floored to the nearest integer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e22ff6fc321d7eede1c2519238ccbc58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-389fa89b589e468d5913361f0a3f42d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD: SIMULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The low score (18.75%) suggests the student may have attempted a simulation-based approach but failed to correctly model the problem's state transitions or iterative behavior, which is common when simulation logic is misunderstood or incomplete."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's simulation is flawed: it only reverses the operations when m &gt; n, but fails to consider cases where m &lt; n and n can be reached by multiplying m by 2 multiple times — the logic incorrectly assumes m must always be reduced, missing the bidirectional nature of possible paths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e3a8b503c95e5635518851840c9288b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab3a2497782f2369f045518e829f36ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD: CONTROL_STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The control structure misses edge cases: it breaks when m is odd and not a perfect square, but does not consider that n might be reachable by increasing m via multiplication (reverse direction not fully explored), leading to incorrect 'No' outputs for valid cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error may stem from incorrect use of control structures (e.g., initializing T=1 inside a loop or conditional), leading to repeated or unintended resets, contributing to the partial correctness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e3a8b503c95e5635518851840c9288b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33b73767750d16af269cfd907acea934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD: INPUT_OUTPUT_AND_SEQUENTIAL_STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The program incorrectly handles the case where n = 0 and m = 0 by returning early without output, and also fails to output anything when n = 0 and m &gt; 0, violating expected I/O behavior — sequential logic is broken in edge case handling."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student likely misapplied sequential flow or input/output handling, as indicated by the low score of 18.75, suggesting improper variable initialization or incorrect order of operations in the program."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's submission includes 'T = 1;' which is likely intended as initialization for test cases, but the error description ('部分正确，得分：18.75') suggests a fundamental misunderstanding in input handling or sequential execution flow, such as failing to read input properly or not looping over multiple test cases correctly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e3a8b503c95e5635518851840c9288b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33b73767750d16af269cfd907acea934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab3a2497782f2369f045518e829f36ba</data>
    </node>
