    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;INPUT_OUTPUT_AND_SEQUENTIAL_STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">90.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红's problem demands precise input parsing and sequential output of swap operations, indicating mastery of I/O and procedural flow is essential for a correct solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem demands precise input parsing and sequential output of swap operations, making this knowledge point critical for correct implementation."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem requires correct input/output flow and sequential processing of array data, which the student program implements correctly with std::cin and std::cout."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题要求处理多组输入，学生程序正确使用了T循环和快速I/O设置，表明对输入输出结构掌握良好。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题明确要求输入数组并按顺序处理，学生正确实现了输入读取和序列排序，表明掌握了基本的输入输出与顺序处理流程。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红’s problem requires sequential input of the matrix and output of swap operations in order, which the student partially implemented but likely with flawed logic, causing the output error."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题要求精确的输入读取和输出格式（交换坐标对），这依赖于正确的输入输出与顺序结构处理能力。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem structure demands strict input parsing and sequential output of swap operations, as reflected in the student's code."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题明确要求按特定格式读取输入和输出交换指令，因此 Input_Output_and_Sequential_Structure 是正确实现其解法的基础。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem requires precise input parsing, sequential processing of swap operations, and correct output formatting of swap pairs, which are all aspects of Input_Output_and_Sequential_Structure that the student's program attempts but fails to implement correctly."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem requires strict sequential processing: reading input, computing swaps, and outputting results in a specific format, which the student’s program attempts to implement with standard I/O and linear execution."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf668f21e72d8570408d55048adcda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03aa5b650266df4503cc3ab5342d2ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fedfd8dc5bb3022a25bfcc5fe660373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b80c66cbff74b6030244a0523bb9e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410c9ee9aeea30ffa768d055e5128a0e</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;ENUMERATION_AND_SORTING&quot;">
      <data key="d3">178.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红's problem implicitly relies on enumerating the positions of '1's and sorting them into the correct quadrant, though the student's code may not implement this correctly."&lt;SEP&gt;The entity "ENUMERATION_AND_SORTING" refers to a foundational computational methodology that is absolutely essential for solving 小红’s problem, which involves transforming a binary matrix so that all '1's are concentrated in the top-left quadrant with the minimum number of operations. This methodology consists of two interdependent, non-negotiable steps: enumeration and sorting.

First, enumeration requires the systematic traversal and identification of all positions in the matrix that contain '1's — and sometimes '0's or other candidate values — to ensure comprehensive coverage of all misplaced elements that must be relocated. This step ensures no relevant element is overlooked in the optimization process.

Second, sorting transforms these enumerated positions into an ordered sequence, typically based on their spatial proximity to or optimal alignment with the target top-left quadrant. This ordering enables the computation of the most efficient relocation strategy, such as minimizing the total number of swap operations or determining median target coordinates for optimal placement. Multiple descriptions confirm that sorting acts as a critical preprocessing step, allowing for strategic reordering of candidate positions to derive minimal-move solutions. Successful student implementations have consistently employed sorting algorithms (e.g., std::sort) to achieve optimal results, while failures are invariably traced to incomplete enumeration or incorrect sorting logic.

All provided descriptions converge on the same conclusion: 小红’s problem implicitly — and necessarily — requires enumerating the positions of all '1's and then sorting them into an optimal sequence for relocation to the top-left quadrant. The unified framework of ENUMERATION_AND_SORTING underpins the entire solution process, integrating exhaustive search (enumeration) with strategic ordering (sorting) to achieve the desired structured output efficiently and reliably. There are no contradictions among the descriptions; rather, they reinforce each other, collectively affirming that ENUMERATION_AND_SORTING is not merely a helpful approach but the indispensable core strategy for any correct and efficient solution to 小红’s problem.&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem necessitates enumerating misplaced '1's and logically ordering their movement to target positions, implying enumeration and sorting are essential to her problem's solution strategy."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa396a1e574085f91576e710eaa87a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e161f201c8def8f1d7dafe61f19dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7ab6a56958755965617c1147a388579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4565bd13d40f1df7dd3737e1885f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fedfd8dc5bb3022a25bfcc5fe660373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b80c66cbff74b6030244a0523bb9e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410c9ee9aeea30ffa768d055e5128a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5142f619b26ce2cf4daf48d5ff07040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-491b51dba2652c663fb7ffdf86cf09c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a436263dc7f42b9debfea46e9464a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf668f21e72d8570408d55048adcda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03aa5b650266df4503cc3ab5342d2ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;GREEDY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">166.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The entity "GREEDY" refers to a theoretically optimal algorithmic strategy characterized by making locally optimal choices at each step to achieve a globally optimal solution, and it is the definitive and intentionally designed solution paradigm for all problem variants posed by "小红". In the context of "小红"’s problems, GREEDY is not merely a suggested heuristic but the core principle underlying all correct solutions, explicitly endorsed through problem design and constrained by a maximum operation limit of n³/2, which necessitates minimal, efficient operations such as swaps or adjustments.

In binary array rearrangement tasks, "小红"’s problem expects a greedy approach—each swap should directly reduce the distance of a '1' to its target location in the top-left quadrant to stay within the operation limit. This involves systematically prioritizing the nearest '1' to the target region and advancing it one step at a time, avoiding backtracking and ensuring optimal substructure. This approach guarantees the minimum total number of operations under the given constraints and aligns with the foundational properties of greedy algorithms, where local optimality cumulatively leads to global optimality. The constraint on maximum operations implicitly validates GREEDY as the only feasible optimal solution for such rearrangements.

Beyond binary arrays, GREEDY is central to other problem types designed by "小红". In tasks requiring minimization of total adjustment costs, the greedy strategy dictates selecting the median as the target value to minimize the sum of absolute deviations. In element modification problems, GREEDY requires retaining the two most frequent elements to minimize the number of changes. However, students frequently fail due to implementation errors such as improper global max/min updates, incomplete enumeration of valid median candidates, or failure to exhaustively evaluate all valid pairs of frequent elements—revealing a common misunderstanding of the strategy’s rigorous requirements.

Across all variants—whether involving positional optimization in binary arrays, statistical centering via median selection, or frequency-based element retention—GREEDY is the unequivocal and intended algorithmic framework. While students consistently attempt to apply greedy principles, recurring implementation flaws—including incorrect state management, incomplete enumeration, or misinterpretation of optimality conditions—demonstrate that the theoretical soundness of GREEDY is well-established, but its practical execution demands precise and meticulous application. Thus, "小红"’s problems are explicitly structured to validate and reinforce GREEDY as the optimal solution paradigm, with student errors serving as indicators of common misconceptions in implementing the</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa396a1e574085f91576e710eaa87a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4565bd13d40f1df7dd3737e1885f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fedfd8dc5bb3022a25bfcc5fe660373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b80c66cbff74b6030244a0523bb9e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410c9ee9aeea30ffa768d055e5128a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5142f619b26ce2cf4daf48d5ff07040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-491b51dba2652c663fb7ffdf86cf09c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a436263dc7f42b9debfea46e9464a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03aa5b650266df4503cc3ab5342d2ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;CONTROL_STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">82.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红's problem demands precise control flow to iterate over possible subarrays and update extremal values; the student uses loops and functions correctly but misapplies the logic for boundary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题需要精确的分支逻辑来处理数组分割和中位数选择，学生程序中存在逻辑错误（如a[mid[1]]非法索引），表明控制结构使用不当。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题需要条件分支判断（如中位数是否相等）和循环计数，学生代码中存在控制结构，但逻辑错误（如cnt1--）表明对控制流理解有误。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题结构要求复杂的条件分支处理（如奇偶长度分区），学生使用了if-else和循环控制结构，但逻辑错误导致结果不正确。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红’s problem demands precise control flow to iterate until the matrix is corrected, but the student’s code snippet lacks internal control logic, indicating incomplete grasp of the required loop and condition structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题需要精确的控制流（如嵌套循环和条件判断）来定位错误位置的'1'并控制交换次数，因此Control_Structure是实现逻辑的核心。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem requires control structures to manage multiple test cases and iterative swap logic, as seen in the student's main loop."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem demands precise control over the sequence of swaps and conditional movement logic, which is implemented through nested loops and state variables like cnti and cntj in the student's code."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题要求程序具备清晰的控制结构（循环、条件判断）以管理多次交换操作和输出序列，因此 Control_Structure 是实现其解法的必要知识。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem requires control structures to manage multiple test cases and iterative swap generation, as seen in the student’s main loop structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"小红's problem demands precise control structures to iterate through matrix indices, manage nested loops, and reset counters (e.g., cnti, cntj), which are directly reflected in the student's code structure."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf668f21e72d8570408d55048adcda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b80c66cbff74b6030244a0523bb9e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03aa5b650266df4503cc3ab5342d2ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e161f201c8def8f1d7dafe61f19dc1</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;双生数组&quot;">
      <data key="d3">97.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红定义了'双生数组'的概念，并以此作为算法问题的核心目标，是该事件的创造者和驱动者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了'双生数组'这一概念，并以此作为算法问题的目标，是该事件的创造者和驱动者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了‘双生数组’这一概念，是该事件的创造者和问题设定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了‘双生数组’这一概念，是该事件的提出者和规则制定者，直接关联其逻辑构造。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了'双生数组'的概念，并以此作为算法问题的求解目标，是该事件的创造者和驱动者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了'双生数组'这一概念，是该事件的提出者和规则制定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了'双生数组'的概念，是该事件的创造者和问题设定者，直接构建了问题的核心目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了‘双生数组’的概念，并以此作为问题的核心目标，是该事件的创造者和驱动者。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641cef19afae4c546ffa6d06efbe027f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5142f619b26ce2cf4daf48d5ff07040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-491b51dba2652c663fb7ffdf86cf09c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f71d63af657c5508ccdab07ea6c18f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;BINARY_SEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红的问题中，目标值的最优选择具有单调性，适合二分搜索，但学生完全未使用该方法，显示对优化搜索空间的意识缺失。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题本可通过二分查找最优目标值来解决，但学生错误地尝试手动计算多个中位数候选，表明对 Binary_Search 的理解不完整或误用。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红的问题在理论上允许使用二分搜索优化目标值查找，但学生未采用，说明该知识点是潜在优化方向，未被学生识别。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;DYNAMIC_PROGRAMMING&quot;">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红的问题具有动态规划的潜力（如子问题：前i个元素中选一个目标值），但学生未采用DP，而是使用不完整的贪心方法，表明未识别该问题的DP结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"虽然 Dynamic_Programming 可用于此问题，但小红的题目设计更倾向于贪心与排序解法，学生也未使用 DP，因此该知识点未被涉及。"&lt;SEP&gt;"虽然小红的问题可被DP解决，但学生未使用DP，说明该知识点虽相关，但未被学生掌握或应用，是问题设计中可选的高级解法。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;SIMULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">174.0</data>
      <data key="d4">小红设计了一个核心为模拟任务的计算问题，要求求解者通过逐次模拟相邻元素（或字符）的交换操作，将初始矩阵逐步转换为目标状态——“好矩阵”。多个描述一致强调，Simulation（模拟）是解决该问题的中心计算技术、核心算法方法与关键知识领域，其本质在于建模并执行一系列相邻交换的序列过程，以达成目标矩阵结构。尽管部分学生尝试采用数学推导（如计算候选值的总绝对差或利用中位数优化）来近似模拟变换的代价，这些方法仍被视为对模拟思维的初步应用，并未取代模拟作为问题设计的本意。然而，学生在实现过程中存在错误，例如因中位数选择不当导致模拟目标偏离，反映出对模拟目的的理解偏差。虽然有少数描述声称最优解无需逐次模拟，或学生未采用模拟方法，但这些说法与其他多数权威描述中“模拟是核心”的结论相矛盾；综合判断，该问题的设计初衷明确要求通过模拟相邻交换来实现状态转换，学生实现中的偏差恰恰印证了模拟思维在问题解决中的必要性与直接相关性。因此，尽管存在实现层面的优化尝试与执行错误，小红的问题本质上仍是一个以“模拟相邻交换”为必要手段的计算任务，Simulation 是其不可替代的核心方法。</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa396a1e574085f91576e710eaa87a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51fa172e57c73db466ea836759cfee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e161f201c8def8f1d7dafe61f19dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd847ee4bb18545e7523cd52f77dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7ab6a56958755965617c1147a388579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4565bd13d40f1df7dd3737e1885f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e600afd93ca192eb8ffc6cb8cc292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fedfd8dc5bb3022a25bfcc5fe660373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e71bd5f93d74a52e913bc532b569f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410c9ee9aeea30ffa768d055e5128a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5142f619b26ce2cf4daf48d5ff07040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a436263dc7f42b9debfea46e9464a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf668f21e72d8570408d55048adcda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03aa5b650266df4503cc3ab5342d2ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;HASH&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红的问题要求高效统计元素出现次数，学生使用unordered_map实现哈希计数，符合问题对效率的需求，体现该知识点的必要性。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c5142f619b26ce2cf4daf48d5ff07040</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;好矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d3">321.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红定义了‘好矩阵’的数学条件，是该事件的创造者和问题设定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;小红是“好矩阵”这一概念的定义者、提出者、创造者和规则制定者，全面构建了其理论基础与实施框架。她不仅首次定义了“好矩阵”的数学条件，还系统性地确立了其数学结构、转换目标、构造规则与转化标准，贯穿了从理论抽象到操作规范的全过程。作为该事件的创始者与问题设计者，小红设定了“好矩阵”的核心逻辑、运作机制与目标状态，其工作涵盖了概念的提出、规则体系的建立、结构的构建以及转化路径的规划，使“好矩阵”成为一个完整、自洽且可操作的数学框架。所有描述一致表明，小红是“好矩阵”从无到有的唯一源头，其贡献覆盖了定义、设计、规则制定与目标设定的全部关键维度，主导了该概念的诞生与演化。&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了‘好矩阵’的数学条件，是该事件的提出者和规则制定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了‘好矩阵’的数学结构和转换目标，是该事件的提出者和规则制定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了‘好矩阵’的数学结构和转换目标，是该事件的发起者和规则制定者。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf3655e2f9ff0ad97a40cbb5e827990f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61e13a3e834268dd3e41a7d76eb91d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa396a1e574085f91576e710eaa87a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c45ae6d217837b0ec49eaf31b3f5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd98342443974d00046bbc62a7ae1f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa22c7c6b0ee550d684fbba16cdd447e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e161f201c8def8f1d7dafe61f19dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7ab6a56958755965617c1147a388579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84eba6b6eff8493a43c7fd384677acc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4565bd13d40f1df7dd3737e1885f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fedfd8dc5bb3022a25bfcc5fe660373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a588519a4b977de5b0bcf8ded42f8642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410c9ee9aeea30ffa768d055e5128a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6ae6c968489276c8bb614966bd0f46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf205584a12138b86107f950268b071f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dd2069b32b3ad84665dc044ac51f497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-167bf23db68d82578bef6b617284955f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f97b7273e9cd49bbbd3b2dcef862908b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e4b814718769c7c5ff34fd8d9992e16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7505a8a58bc2ae0a0f49a4f4a99ca45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f273c58705b21c2ef1fc6c43ff66b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a436263dc7f42b9debfea46e9464a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf668f21e72d8570408d55048adcda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246822371b4a88626131f0e16a7011d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acfb1c8a2a7c5ab2297cc1bce76d8554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60231925bd696a34976f33351b0f3da8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd35d2da3ec05d7b2e867504beda050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cdb2064474980b06343cd68cff259c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03aa5b650266df4503cc3ab5342d2ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;N行N列01矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红持有并操作给定的n行n列01矩阵，目标是将其转换为她所定义的好矩阵。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红持有并要求处理一个给定的n行n列01矩阵，将其转化为好矩阵，是问题的发起者和操作对象关联者。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9dd2069b32b3ad84665dc044ac51f497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf205584a12138b86107f950268b071f</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;N 行 N 列矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d3">26.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红定义了该矩阵的结构和‘好矩阵’的判定标准，是问题的发起者和规则制定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红定义了该矩阵的结构和转化目标，是问题的提出者和规则制定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红提供了一个具体的01矩阵作为输入，要求将其转换为‘好矩阵’，因此她与该数据结构有直接关联。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f7559a33bedc5f901d766c18542da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4524936a6b8c2ae52a229c861568c00f</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;相邻字符交换操作&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红设定了仅允许相邻字符交换作为转化矩阵的唯一操作方式，是问题约束的核心。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-4524936a6b8c2ae52a229c861568c00f</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;小红&quot;" target="&quot;N 行 N 列 01 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d3">57.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小红拥有并操作该矩阵，目标是将其转换为'好矩阵'，是问题的主体与目标对象之间的关联。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红拥有并操作该矩阵，要求将其转化为她定义的好矩阵，是问题的发起者与目标设定者。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红持有并操作一个初始的 n 行 n 列 01 矩阵，目标是将其转变为好矩阵，因此她与该结构存在直接的输入与转化关系。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红持有并操作一个初始的 n×n 01 矩阵，目标是将其转换为‘好矩阵’，表明她与该数据结构有直接关联。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红持有并操作一个初始的 n×n 01 矩阵，目标是将其转化为‘好矩阵’。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红持有并操作一个 n 行 n 列的 01 矩阵，目标是将其转化为‘好矩阵’，因此她与该数据结构存在直接的处理关系。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小红持有并操作一个给定的 01 矩阵，目标是将其转化为好矩阵，表明她与该结构存在直接的处理关系。"</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c84eba6b6eff8493a43c7fd384677acc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c45ae6d217837b0ec49eaf31b3f5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246822371b4a88626131f0e16a7011d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd35d2da3ec05d7b2e867504beda050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cdb2064474980b06343cd68cff259c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f97b7273e9cd49bbbd3b2dcef862908b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6ae6c968489276c8bb614966bd0f46</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
