      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program attempts to assign values from 1 \sim n to positions, but its greedy approach may skip valid assignments, leading to incomplete permutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Student Program implicitly assumes values from 1 to n are to be assigned, but fails to ensure all values in this range are used due to incorrect greedy logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student’s program assigns values from 1 to n in ascending order to satisfy the permutation requirement, directly using this range as the source of values."</data>
