    <edge source="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;KNOWLEDGE POINTS TO EXTRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">76.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The error description identifies a student's incorrect implementation, which must be analyzed against the listed knowledge points to determine which computational concepts the student misunderstood or applied incorrectly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is analyzed against the Knowledge Points to Extract list to determine which algorithmic concepts the student misunderstood or applied incorrectly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is analyzed against the Knowledge Points to Extract list to determine which algorithmic concepts the student misunderstood or applied incorrectly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is evaluated against the Knowledge Points to Extract list to determine which algorithmic concepts the student misunderstood or applied incorrectly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is used to evaluate the student's mastery of specific knowledge points from the provided list, identifying which algorithmic or programming concepts were misapplied."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is used to evaluate the student's mastery of the knowledge points listed, identifying which algorithmic concepts the student misunderstood or applied incorrectly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is used to evaluate the student's mastery of the knowledge points listed, determining whether their understanding of specific computational concepts is good or bad based on their incorrect implementation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is evaluated against the Knowledge Points to Extract list to determine which algorithmic concepts the student misunderstood or applied incorrectly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The error description is analyzed against the Knowledge Points list to determine which algorithmic concepts the student misunderstood or applied incorrectly."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-52543ca7da1d4a9ba677841843749191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3be5d2e7b4cdc0624a78ec7eea0965b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc4bde127c899173d8ce8f82274102b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6bef65f0a968ef3a0849ac39bbd081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d92e16219582b9326647688714ca17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb62e57098228f41920f39d20ae4d2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88fa16b4f4700aea35ca6e79d0208cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0578a35809a5b5cc19052ef0d6078e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45490059e4c46d4b5d35da604f2ccf3f</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;DYNAMIC_PROGRAMMING&quot;">
      <data key="d3">34.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The absence of memoization or subproblem reuse in the student’s code suggests they may not recognize this as a dynamic programming problem, or incorrectly assumed a brute-force enumeration approach was sufficient."&lt;SEP&gt;"The structure resembles a DP state update (combining subproblems via Min and Cnt), but the incorrect answer indicates misunderstanding of recurrence or state dependency."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student’s error in handling array bounds (e.g., j + i - 1 &gt; m) indicates a misunderstanding in dynamic programming state transitions for diagonal sums."&lt;SEP&gt;"The use of Min and Cnt with arithmetic combinations suggests an attempt at dynamic optimization; the student likely misdefined state transitions or recurrence relations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The use of 'f' and 'cnt' variables suggests an attempt to track subproblem states, but the logic is not properly accumulated or reset, indicating a misunderstanding of dynamic state management."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-583327d1ca0d6043bcd282a108af1a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6bef65f0a968ef3a0849ac39bbd081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d92e16219582b9326647688714ca17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88fa16b4f4700aea35ca6e79d0208cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0578a35809a5b5cc19052ef0d6078e7a</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;GOOD: [DESCRIPTION]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"When the error description contains no errors or affirmations like 'No error', it is classified as 'Good: [description]', indicating correct understanding."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c7258c56b189afe5558686950c289cc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;BAD: [DESCRIPTION]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"When the error description includes specific mistakes or inaccuracies, it is classified as 'Bad: [description]', indicating misunderstanding."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c7258c56b189afe5558686950c289cc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;GOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"An absence of error details in the error description leads to the 'Good' classification, indicating understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"The absence of an error description leads to the 'Good' classification, indicating no misunderstandings were detected."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-ccea04d305753de718ec8196bbb4d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;BAD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">55.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"'Bad' is the prefix used in the error description to signal a misunderstanding, making it an essential structural component of the error format."&lt;SEP&gt;"The presence of an error description triggers the 'Bad' classification, indicating a misunderstanding or incorrect application."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'Bad' label is always accompanied by an error description that explains the nature of the student's misunderstanding or incorrect answer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'Bad' indicator is explicitly tied to the presence of an error description, signaling a student’s misunderstanding or incorrect application of knowledge."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Error Description is the textual evidence that triggers the 'Bad' classification in the assessment system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The presence of error details in the error description triggers the 'Bad' classification, indicating misunderstanding."</data>
