    <edge source="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;SIMULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">99.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The code attempts to simulate a grid-based condition (checking rows, columns, diagonals for values &gt; 1), but the counting logic (cnt) is broken due to improper flag reuse and scope, showing a flawed simulation implementation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code simulates a computational process using counters and arithmetic (Min, Cnt, x, y), and the error suggests the simulation logic is incorrectly implemented."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code simulates a mathematical accumulation process using Min, Cnt, x, and y; the error suggests the simulation logic does not correctly model the intended problem behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student attempted to simulate a grid-based constraint system (checking rows, columns, diagonals for values &gt; 1), but the logic for flag and cnt updates is flawed, indicating misunderstanding of the simulation's intended behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code attempts to simulate checking matrix conditions for a diagonal or pattern, but the logic fails due to incorrect index calculation, indicating poor simulation design."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code attempts to simulate grid-based conditions (e.g., checking a[k][3-k+1] and a[i][k]), but the student’s logic for setting flags and counters is flawed, indicating poor simulation design."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code simulates a grid-based condition check (e.g., diagonals, rows, columns), but the implementation is incorrect, suggesting poor understanding of simulation logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code attempts to simulate a grid-based condition check (e.g., a[k][3-k+1]), which is a simulation of a diagonal or matrix traversal, but the logic is flawed, indicating poor simulation design."&lt;SEP&gt;"The problem requires simulating matrix traversal and condition evaluation, which the student implemented incorrectly, failing to properly check diagonal and row/column constraints."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student’s code attempts to simulate matrix condition checks (e.g., a[k][3-k+1], a[i][k], a[k][j]), but fails, showing poor understanding of simulation logic in grid-based problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student attempted to simulate a matrix-based condition check but failed to correctly implement the logic, resulting in an incorrect answer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The problem involves simulating a grid-based condition check (e.g., diagonal and row/column traversal), but the student’s logic fails to correctly implement the simulation, leading to incorrect flag setting."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-52543ca7da1d4a9ba677841843749191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9ae7a51aebab6821f40062b4d3226b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583327d1ca0d6043bcd282a108af1a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3be5d2e7b4cdc0624a78ec7eea0965b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc4bde127c899173d8ce8f82274102b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc13f3cc7f5b3af45d1ad4e19c942b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b2c89ce18073790268729bdeee92b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d92e16219582b9326647688714ca17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb62e57098228f41920f39d20ae4d2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88fa16b4f4700aea35ca6e79d0208cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0578a35809a5b5cc19052ef0d6078e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45490059e4c46d4b5d35da604f2ccf3f</data>
