    <edge source="&quot;ENUMERATION_AND_SORTING&quot;" target="&quot;NUMBER_THEORY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">46.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Enumeration and sorting are used as computational tools to explore number-theoretic properties of pairs (a_i, a_j) under the XOR-GCD constraint."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration of divisors (sorting and iteration) is used to explore number-theoretic properties (GCD) of array elements in the problem solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student combines enumeration/sorting with number theory concepts but fails to correctly integrate them, leading to an incorrect solution despite structural similarity to a valid approach."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration_and_Sorting is used as a computational method to explore solutions grounded in Number_Theory principles, specifically the GCD-XOR relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration_and_Sorting enables systematic testing of pairs under the number-theoretic condition, linking algorithmic structure with mathematical constraints."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration_and_Sorting techniques are used in Number_Theory problems to iterate over integer ranges or sort divisors/factors systematically."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-dc35810a6d5ed3f74124a2343a41baf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96a5a90585cd28544500c57e9d99022f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ea155f37a5b0dedc89550cd089887dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e323f51098edcf47a15008673b8c96b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2545f92f06987124bd5e6a93af6ed19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f879cfc3be84369f4b6a9265d25a34</data>
