      <data key="d3">36.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Control structures (if conditions and flags) determine when enumeration steps are triggered or skipped, showing that enumeration is conditional and guided by control logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control_Structure enables enumeration of grid cells and applies sorting (std::min) to select optimal component based on size and adjacent zero count."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration of matrix positions is orchestrated by control structures that manage iteration and state progression (e.g., cnti, cntj), ensuring systematic coverage of the grid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control structures (nested loops) enable the enumeration of all grid positions, making control flow foundational to the enumeration process."</data>
