    <edge source="&quot;ENUMERATION_AND_SORTING&quot;" target="&quot;SEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d3">69.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Enumeration enables the search over matrix elements; the student’s error in enumeration directly impacts the correctness of the search."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration of array elements is used to perform the search for values &gt; 1; the flawed enumeration leads to incorrect search results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration through matrix indices is employed to perform searches for values &gt; 1; the failure to isolate search conditions per dimension (row, column, diagonal) leads to cumulative errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration_and_Sorting often includes Search as a subcomponent, particularly in ordered data processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration_and_Sorting often precedes or enables efficient Search algorithms, as sorting is a prerequisite for binary search and ordered traversal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sorting is often a prerequisite for efficient search algorithms like binary search."&lt;SEP&gt;"The search is implemented via enumeration—iterating over all possible indices to find qualifying conditions—making enumeration the mechanism by which search is carried out."&lt;SEP&gt;"The exhaustive enumeration of grid cells constitutes a form of search, though not algorithmic search; the relationship is conceptual but not technical."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enumeration through loops is used as the mechanism to perform the search over matrix elements."</data>
