      <data key="d4">"Simulation is a core required skill for this problem, and the student's error confirms they lack proficiency in simulating matrix-based logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is a key knowledge point referenced in the list and is the primary technique being applied in the student's code."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is a listed knowledge point and is the core approach of the student’s code, which fails due to incorrect step-by-step logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is applicable as the student's approach mimics matrix construction with dynamic assignment, showing basic familiarity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is listed as a knowledge point and aligns with the step-by-step arithmetic computation in the code, which is likely the core of the student's misunderstanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is listed as a relevant knowledge point, indicating the problem requires step-by-step computational modeling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is explicitly relevant as the code attempts to simulate a grid-based constraint-checking process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is a key knowledge point relevant to the problem’s context, and the student’s flawed code indicates poor mastery of this area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is directly relevant because the code simulates checking a grid for specific conditions, a common problem type in this category."</data>
