    <edge source="&quot;NUMBER_THEORY&quot;" target="&quot;小苯&quot;">
      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小苯 attempts to apply number theory (GCD and XOR relationship) but misapplies it, as seen in the incorrect condition ((a[i] ^ j) &lt; a[i]) and lack of proper GCD computation."&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯's problem requires computing GCD and relating it to XOR, which are fundamental number theory concepts; the student attempts to leverage this relationship but incorrectly implements the logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯's solution hinges on understanding the mathematical properties of GCD and XOR, core concepts in number theory, though the implementation contains errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯's algorithm implicitly depends on number-theoretic properties of GCD and XOR, though the implementation contains errors in how these properties are applied."&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯 correctly uses GCD in the condition a_i XOR a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j), but the implementation does not properly compute or validate GCD for all divisor pairs, indicating partial understanding."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-dc35810a6d5ed3f74124a2343a41baf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96a5a90585cd28544500c57e9d99022f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ea155f37a5b0dedc89550cd089887dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2545f92f06987124bd5e6a93af6ed19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f879cfc3be84369f4b6a9265d25a34</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NUMBER_THEORY&quot;" target="&quot;HASH&quot;">
      <data key="d3">111.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Hash functions depend on Number_Theory principles to guarantee one-wayness and resistance to preimage attacks, forming a core dependency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hash functions rely on modular arithmetic and prime number properties from Number Theory to ensure uniformity and collision resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hash is used to optimize the application of number-theoretic properties (GCD) by avoiding recomputation across duplicate values."&lt;SEP&gt;"The number-theoretic condition (a_i XOR a_j == GCD(a_i,a_j)) is checked using a hash table (cnt[]) to quickly verify if a complementary value exists in the array."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number Theory provides the mathematical foundation for cryptographic hash functions, making it essential to the design and security of hashing algorithms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number Theory underpins many cryptographic hash functions, suggesting a foundational relationship in algorithmic design."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number_Theory provides foundational concepts (e.g., modular arithmetic, primality) that underpin the design and security of hash functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number_Theory provides the mathematical foundation (e.g., prime factorization, modular inverses) essential for constructing secure and collision-resistant hash functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hash functions often rely on number-theoretic principles such as modular arithmetic and prime numbers for distribution and collision resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hash functions often rely on number-theoretic principles such as modular arithmetic and prime number properties for collision resistance and distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hash functions rely on number-theoretic concepts like modular arithmetic, prime numbers, and integer divisibility to ensure uniform distribution and collision resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hashing is often used in Number Theory problems to store and quickly retrieve modular results or large integer states."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number_Theory concepts like modular arithmetic are often used in designing hash functions and avoiding collisions in competitive programming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number theory concepts like modular arithmetic are used in designing hash functions to minimize collisions."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7f055e23ba597a3dd42758c3042cf0a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28265c866810ef692fe55afa50800419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96a5a90585cd28544500c57e9d99022f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0f812fb277db80b9e528ec9d8f328f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e323f51098edcf47a15008673b8c96b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174ed570d15fd77291044f9539d0d3fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2545f92f06987124bd5e6a93af6ed19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f307959a2f0f81a0f2df84db59d9b2e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80238b5fffb44ffa0ed8e2b2ac553255</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
