    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GREEDY&quot;" target="&quot;好矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d3">125.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The entity "GREEDY" refers to an optimal and efficient strategy for constructing the "好矩阵" (good matrix), a problem that involves repositioning all '1's in a binary matrix to achieve a desired configuration—typically concentrated in the top-left quadrant—with minimal total swaps. The greedy approach to this problem involves iteratively moving each '1' directly along the shortest possible path toward its designated target position in the top-left quadrant, without unnecessary or backtracking moves. This strategy is consistently described across all sources as the most efficient method, ensuring that the total number of swaps remains within the operational bound of n³/2, a critical constraint in the problem’s formulation.

While one description notes that a greedy strategy “may fail due to blocking or suboptimal ordering,” the overwhelming consensus among the provided descriptions resolves this potential contradiction by emphasizing that, in the context of the 好矩阵 problem, the greedy method is not only effective but optimal. The structure of the problem—where each '1' has a well-defined target region (the top-left quadrant) and the goal is to minimize total moves—naturally supports a greedy solution. By prioritizing the relocation of each '1' to its nearest valid target position in sequence, the greedy algorithm avoids complex global optimization, reduces computational overhead, and guarantees feasibility within the operation limit.

Thus, the greedy strategy is not merely a heuristic but the theoretically and practically optimal approach for constructing 好矩阵. It aligns with the problem’s inherent constraints and objectives, ensuring minimal total swaps, direct pathing, and efficient convergence. The term "GREEDY" in this context is synonymous with the optimal algorithm for 好矩阵 construction, as repeatedly affirmed by multiple descriptions that characterize it as efficient, direct, minimal in operation count, and fully compliant with the n³/2 swap constraint.</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-6247e0c09a8368e71631b60beb57a0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f6856b0857c340a0a736de1a173d764&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f273c58705b21c2ef1fc6c43ff66b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4565bd13d40f1df7dd3737e1885f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf205584a12138b86107f950268b071f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a436263dc7f42b9debfea46e9464a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa396a1e574085f91576e710eaa87a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5448b6a1f2bc39e282db3976a922f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e8638ebdbdf00618c1aeeebfe5c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd98342443974d00046bbc62a7ae1f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fedfd8dc5bb3022a25bfcc5fe660373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e400700ddd5c7295c464b96b4722c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410c9ee9aeea30ffa768d055e5128a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GREEDY&quot;" target="&quot;相邻字符交换操作&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The greedy approach relies entirely on adjacent swaps to achieve local optimization, making the operation the atomic unit of the greedy strategy."</data>
