      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Both Greedy and Dynamic_Programming are algorithmic strategies for optimization; Greedy makes immediate optimal choices while Dynamic_Programming considers all subproblems, making them conceptually related but distinct approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both Greedy and Dynamic_Programming are event-based algorithmic strategies used in optimization; Greedy prioritizes immediate gains while Dynamic_Programming explores all substructures, making them competing yet related approaches in problem-solving events."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both are algorithmic paradigms used for optimization, but Greedy makes local choices while Dynamic_Programming considers global substructure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greedy and Dynamic_Programming are both optimization paradigms; Greedy is a subset of DP in cases where local optima guarantee global optima."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both are algorithmic paradigms for optimization; greedy makes local choices while dynamic programming considers global subproblems."</data>
