    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;(X+1,Y+1)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">56.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"(x+1,y+1) is a direct propagation direction of Dragon's Breath flame, forming one arm of the 'X' pattern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dragon's Breath flame extends in the (x+1,y+1) direction diagonally across the grid, destroying monsters along that path."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dragon's Breath propagates along the (x+1,y+1) direction from its center, destroying monsters in that diagonal line as part of its 'X' shape."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dragon's Breath propagates flame along the (x+1,y+1) diagonal direction, destroying all monsters on that line from the firing point."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dragon's Breath propagates flame along the diagonal direction (x+1,y+1) from the target, destroying all monsters along that line."&lt;SEP&gt;"(x+1,y+1) is a directional extension point of Dragon's Breath flame, contributing to the 'X' shaped destruction pattern on the grid."</data>
