      <data key="d4">"sum[1][i] precomputes diagonal sums that correspond to another arm of the Dragon's Breath 'X' pattern."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9dfc436139fa6006082f3b7f4127742f</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;SUM2[0][I]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[0][i] precomputes diagonal sums that correspond to a third arm of the Dragon's Breath 'X' pattern."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9dfc436139fa6006082f3b7f4127742f</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;SUM2[1][I]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[1][i] precomputes diagonal sums that correspond to the fourth arm of the Dragon's Breath 'X' pattern."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9dfc436139fa6006082f3b7f4127742f</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;SUM[2][M]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum[2][M] stores precomputed diagonal sums used by the Dragon's Breath algorithm to efficiently determine maximum damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"sum[2][M] stores precomputed diagonal sums used to efficiently calculate the total monsters defeated by Dragon's Breath."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-0abd9d06cc1108aa2d33d0668e3a2f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04d5bda19778e26fdcdbd138b92cbbe2</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;SUM2[2][M]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[2][M] stores precomputed diagonal sums for the other two diagonal directions, enabling full coverage of Dragon's Breath impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"sum2[2][M] stores precomputed diagonal sums from bottom-to-top directions, completing the full coverage needed to evaluate all possible Dragon's Breath trajectories."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-0abd9d06cc1108aa2d33d0668e3a2f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04d5bda19778e26fdcdbd138b92cbbe2</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;TMP&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"tmp is used in the program to compute the total monster count destroyed by Dragon's Breath at a specific target, simulating the ability's effect."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-16239776332d396b902352ee025093cf</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;SUM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Sum is the runtime variable used to compute the total monsters along a diagonal path during Dragon's Breath evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-04d5bda19778e26fdcdbd138b92cbbe2</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DRAGON'S BREATH&quot;" target="&quot;SUM OF MONSTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dragon's Breath directly calculates and destroys the Sum of Monsters along its diagonal paths, making this sum the measurable outcome of the event."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c4a7b2a080725c29db421d4e4ace60f7</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRID MAP&quot;" target="&quot;A_{I,J}&quot;">
      <data key="d3">39.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Grid Map's monster distribution is fully described by the values of a_{i,j} at each coordinate (i,j), making it the data representation of the map."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_{i,j} is the data structure embedded in the Grid Map that quantifies monster density at each cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_{i,j} defines the monster density at each cell (i,j) of the Grid Map, forming the data structure upon which Dragon's Breath calculations are based."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_{i,j} provides the monster count data for each cell in the Grid Map, essential for calculating Dragon's Breath effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-0abd9d06cc1108aa2d33d0668e3a2f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfc436139fa6006082f3b7f4127742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79d74783b73ceb32dae708b26591e446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04d5bda19778e26fdcdbd138b92cbbe2</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRID MAP&quot;" target="&quot;B[M][M]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"b[M][M] is a temporary transposed version of the Grid Map used when n &gt; m to simplify computation."&lt;SEP&gt;"b[M][M] is used to temporarily store the original Grid Map data during transposition when n &gt; m, ensuring correct diagonal calculation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-0abd9d06cc1108aa2d33d0668e3a2f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04d5bda19778e26fdcdbd138b92cbbe2</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRID MAP&quot;" target="&quot;SUM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum is a computational structure derived from the Grid Map to enable efficient diagonal range sum queries for Dragon's Breath damage calculation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-16239776332d396b902352ee025093cf</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRID MAP&quot;" target="&quot;SUM2&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2 is a computational structure derived from the Grid Map to handle edge cases where Dragon's Breath diagonals extend beyond grid boundaries."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-16239776332d396b902352ee025093cf</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRID MAP&quot;" target="&quot;SUM OF MONSTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Grid Map provides the spatial structure and monster data (a_{i,j}) that determine the possible Sum of Monsters for any Dragon's Breath activation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c4a7b2a080725c29db421d4e4ace60f7</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM&quot;" target="&quot;CODE EXECUTION ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The error likely stems from improper handling of the Sum variable, which is reused across loops without reinitialization in some branches, causing incorrect accumulation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM&quot;" target="&quot;A[U][V]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Sum accumulates values from a[u][v] during diagonal traversals, making it directly dependent on correct array indexing."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM&quot;" target="&quot;U&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Sum accumulates values based on u's trajectory; if u is improperly modified, Sum will reflect incorrect cumulative totals."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM&quot;" target="&quot;V&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Sum's value is directly affected by v's changes during diagonal traversal; unbounded v leads to invalid data being summed."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM&quot;" target="&quot;SUM2&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The temporary variable 'sum' is reused to compute intermediate diagonal sums that are assigned to sum2[0][i] and sum2[1][i]."&lt;SEP&gt;"sum and sum2 are complementary data structures in the student's program, where sum handles in-bound diagonals and sum2 handles out-of-bound diagonals for accurate damage calculation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-16239776332d396b902352ee025093cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97fb25c01f1eb3aee703f8014c736f96</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM&quot;" target="&quot;SUM1&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The temporary variable 'sum' is used to compute intermediate diagonal sums that are then assigned to sum1[1][i]."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-97fb25c01f1eb3aee703f8014c736f96</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM[1][I]&quot;" target="&quot;CODE EXECUTION ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The assignment to sum[1][i] depends on a while loop that may not terminate correctly due to missing bounds checks, resulting in incorrect or undefined values."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM[1][I]&quot;" target="&quot;A[U][V]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum[1][i] is populated by summing a[u][v] along a specific diagonal, so its correctness depends entirely on accurate traversal of a[u][v]."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM[1][I]&quot;" target="&quot;I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum[1][i] is indexed by i, which iterates over columns; if i exceeds array bounds or sum is undersized, this causes memory corruption."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM2[0][I]&quot;" target="&quot;CODE EXECUTION ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[0][i] is calculated using a loop that decrements u and v without checking for underflow, likely causing negative indices and segmentation faults."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM2[0][I]&quot;" target="&quot;A[U][V]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[0][i] depends on summing a[u][v] along the anti-diagonal from top-left downward, but unbounded decrements break memory safety."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM2[0][I]&quot;" target="&quot;I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[0][i] depends on i for column indexing, but i’s range is not validated against sum2’s dimensions, risking buffer overflow."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM2[1][I]&quot;" target="&quot;CODE EXECUTION ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[1][i] is computed using a loop with inconsistent termination conditions (u &amp;&amp; v &lt;= m), which may lead to invalid memory access or incorrect sums."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM2[1][I]&quot;" target="&quot;A[U][V]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[1][i] relies on correct diagonal traversal of a[u][v] from bottom-left to top-right; any index error corrupts the result."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUM2[1][I]&quot;" target="&quot;I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"sum2[1][i] uses i as a column index; if i is not constrained by m or sum2 is not properly allocated, this leads to undefined behavior."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CODE EXECUTION ERROR&quot;" target="&quot;A[U][V]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The error is caused by unbounded access to a[u][v] in while loops where u and v may go out of valid array bounds, leading to runtime crashes."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CODE EXECUTION ERROR&quot;" target="&quot;U&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The runtime error is directly caused by u being decremented without bounds checking, leading to negative indices and invalid memory access."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CODE EXECUTION ERROR&quot;" target="&quot;V&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"v is incremented and decremented in multiple loops without consistent bounds validation, causing out-of-range array access and contributing to the execution error."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A[U][V]&quot;" target="&quot;U&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"u directly indexes the row of array a[u][v]; incorrect manipulation of u leads to invalid memory access in the array."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A[U][V]&quot;" target="&quot;V&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"v directly indexes the column of array a[u][v]; uncontrolled increments/decrements of v cause unsafe array accesses."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-7eae5d00111387ffd168e8ec3f83adc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;RECORD ID: 80-2&quot;" target="&quot;2025-02-06 14:03:57&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The timestamp 2025-02-06 14:03:57 is directly associated with Record ID: 80-2 as its recorded submission time, linking the event to its temporal context."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c7258c56b189afe5558686950c289cc0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GOOD&quot;" target="&quot;RECORD ID: 81-2&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The 'Good' marker is applied to Record ID: 81-2 to indicate the student's correct understanding in this specific submission."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GOOD&quot;" target="&quot;NO ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">58.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"'No Error' is a direct textual trigger that results in the 'Good' classification, indicating the student correctly understood the concept."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' directly corresponds to the 'Good' label, both indicating the absence of mistakes and correct understanding in a student's submission."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' directly triggers the 'Good' marker, indicating the student’s correct understanding without any identified mistakes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The presence of 'No error' in a submission directly triggers the 'Good' evaluation, indicating the student has correctly understood the material."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' is a direct textual trigger that results in the 'Good' classification, indicating the student demonstrated understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"'No error' directly triggers the 'Good' indicator, confirming the student's correct understanding of the problem."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-4aee1cb5b4db6b902a5def2f1b55fc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a3b43879945f4f3f3c62def7b7d32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-448e4914a3aacbe6e90e6ab1a7e58ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174472b84d2963740d25777960a64885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GOOD&quot;" target="&quot;无错误&quot;">
      <data key="d3">54.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"'无错误' is a direct textual trigger in Chinese that results in the 'Good' classification, equivalent to 'No error'."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is a non-English equivalent of 'No Error' and functions identically to trigger the 'Good' classification in multilingual assessment contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is semantically equivalent to 'No error' and similarly triggers the 'Good' marker in multilingual assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chinese phrase '无错误' functions equivalently to 'No error' and is used to trigger the 'Good' evaluation in multilingual contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is the linguistic equivalent of 'No error' and is functionally aligned with the 'Good' label in evaluating student understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"'无错误' is a non-English equivalent of 'No error' and similarly triggers the 'Good' indicator to denote correct performance."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-4aee1cb5b4db6b902a5def2f1b55fc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a3b43879945f4f3f3c62def7b7d32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-448e4914a3aacbe6e90e6ab1a7e58ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174472b84d2963740d25777960a64885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466447976916918cad297fdac172adb1</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GOOD&quot;" target="&quot;NO ERRORS MENTIONED&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"When no errors are mentioned, the system defaults to the 'Good' marker, assuming the submission is correct."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-6be452c5c1988ad6ddd796f64200a752</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
