      <data key="d4">"炸鸡 is the opponent in the tic-tac-toe game who, despite being skilled, allows a rule deviation that could alter the game's outcome."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opponent in the tic-tac-toe game, setting the rules and granting a privilege that may affect the game's strategic balance."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player whose overconfidence leads to the introduction of a special rule in the tic-tac-toe game that alters the game's strategic balance."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game who has introduced a rule modification (double move privilege) that alters the game dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game, relying on optimal play to counter 小L's special privilege and maintain a non-losing position."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game who enforces the special rule, believing their superior skill will still lead to victory."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game who, despite being more skilled, allows a strategic advantage to 小L, influencing the game's outcome dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game who, despite being skilled, allows a strategic advantage to 小L, influencing the game's outcome dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game, whose overconfidence leads to granting 小L a strategic edge, influencing the game's outcome."</data>
